China's AI Ambitions & The Taiwan Question: What It Means for Global Tech & Your Future,"Welcome to Catalyst Conversations with Alex Thorne. In this gripping episode, Alex, Dr. Lena Khan, and cybersecurity expert Ben Carter unravel the complex web connecting China's aggressive pursuit of AI supremacy with the escalating tensions around Taiwan. They break down the strategic implications of Taiwan's dominance in advanced semiconductor manufacturing and how a potential conflict or even economic blockade could send shockwaves through every sector of the global economy, from smartphones to military hardware.

The team dissects China's ""Made in China 2025"" initiative, examining its progress in critical technologies like AI, quantum computing, and advanced robotics, and how these ambitions directly intersect with its geopolitical goals. They discuss the precarious position of global tech giants reliant on Taiwanese chip production, the efforts by the US and Europe to onshore semiconductor manufacturing, and the real risks of a new ""Silicon Curtain"" dividing the world.

