87% of people over 50 have 'degenerative discs' with NO back pain. Read that again.,"Research consistently shows a disconnect between what an MRI reveals and the actual experience of pain. Studies indicate that a vast majority of middle-aged and older adults have findings like disc bulges, herniations, and degenerative changes on their spinal MRIs, yet they experience no pain whatsoever. An MRI is a snapshot of your anatomy, not a predictor of your pain or function. It shows structures, not how those structures are behaving or contributing to your symptoms. Many people with severe, debilitating back pain have completely normal MRIs, while others with significant 'abnormalities' live pain-free lives. It's time to shift focus from imaging labels to understanding your body's true functional capacity. Watch the full video on The Body Whisperer YouTube channel to learn how to interpret your scan results, then take our free 'Spine Decode Quiz' at bodywhisperer.com/decode to get your personalized movement pattern insights in 3 minutes. #BackPain #SpineHealth #MRIResults #PainEducation #PhysicalTherapy",The Body Whisperer | Unraveling Pain Mysteries,315
