What Happens to Your Body After 24 Hours Without Water?,"What would happen if you didn't drink any water for a full day?
In just 2 hours, your urine output drops, and your mouth feels dry.
By 6 hours, you might start feeling fatigued and experience headaches as your body conserves water.
At 12 hours, cognitive function can decline, and your skin loses elasticity. Dizziness becomes more common.
Around 18 hours, muscle cramps and severe fatigue set in. Your blood thickens, straining your heart.
By 24 hours, organ function begins to suffer significantly. Severe dehydration can lead to confusion, kidney stress, and potentially heatstroke.
Water isn't just a drink — it's the foundation of life, keeping every cell in your body functioning.
Stay hydrated! Subscribe for more amazing human body facts and science shorts.

