"Invisible Labour, Visible Waste: Health & Livelihood Challenges for Urban Waste Pickers | Research Talk","Have you ever considered the true cost of urban waste management, beyond what we throw away? While cities grapple with growing mountains of refuse, a hidden workforce of informal waste pickers plays a critical, yet often unacknowledged, role in managing our discards. Join Dr. Lena Kumar as she presents groundbreaking research on the complex health and livelihood challenges faced by thousands of waste pickers in bustling megacities like Mumbai. Many of these individuals, often migrants themselves, live on the margins, contending with hazardous working conditions, lack of social protection, and deep-seated societal prejudices. Through their personal narratives and extensive data, this talk illuminates the precarious existence of those who literally clean up our cities, raising crucial questions about urban sustainability, public health, and social equity. This presentation was delivered on October 20, 2026, as part of our 'Urban Voices' series, highlighting overlooked communities and critical urban issues. Explore more of our research and events at urbanfrontiersinstitute.org",Urban Frontiers Institute,178
