- How Kafka Works: A simple breakdown of its architecture and message flow, highlighting its distributed and fault-tolerant nature.
- Key Use Cases: Discover how Kafka is used for log aggregation, real-time analytics, stream processing, event sourcing, and communication between microservices.
- Advantages of Kafka: Learn about its scalability, durability, high performance, and ability to handle vast amounts of data.
