Distributed Consensus in Edge AI: Mitigating Data Staleness with Lightweight Protocols,"Abstract: Edge AI deployments introduce unique challenges for data consistency, especially when operating on intermittent networks and with diverse data sources. This session will explore the problem of data staleness in distributed edge AI models, where local inference engines process data streams asynchronously. We will present a novel lightweight consensus protocol designed to ensure high data integrity without incurring significant latency or computational overhead, critical for resource-constrained edge devices. Experimental results from a federated learning scenario demonstrate how this protocol effectively reduces staleness and improves model reliability compared to traditional eventual consistency models. The discussion will cover architectural considerations for integrating such protocols into existing edge infrastructure and implications for real-time decision-making systems. Speaker: Dr. Lena Petrova is a lead research scientist at Distributed Intelligence Protocols, specializing in resilient AI systems and edge computing. Her work focuses on developing robust data management strategies for highly distributed and heterogeneous environments. She is a core contributor to several open-source initiatives aimed at enhancing the reliability of AI at the edge and frequently presents at industry and academic conferences on topics related to distributed consensus and data integrity.",Distributed Intelligence Protocols,85
