This project will demonstrate how to build a robust and scalable industrial automation program for sorting applications, covering:

• UDTs (User Defined Data Types) for Part Properties & Station Status
• Global Data Blocks for System Parameters and Configuration
• Conveyor & Gripper State Machine Logic
• Vision System Data Acquisition & Processing
• Recipe Management for Different Part Types
• Comprehensive Fault & Alarm Management

The system involves parts arriving on a main conveyor, being identified by a vision camera, and then sorted into specific bins by a robotic arm or diverter based on their type or quality. This first part focuses on establishing a clean architecture and fundamental programming concepts that can be expanded to:

• Multiple sorting stations
• Advanced quality control checks
• SCADA/HMI integration
• Real-time data logging

This tutorial is perfect for:

