LeetCode 1349 | Maximum Students Taking Exam | DP with Convex Hull Trick | Why Meta Engineers Use This!,"Master the ""Maximum Students Taking Exam"" (LeetCode 1349) LeetCode Hard problem, a challenging example of dynamic programming that frequently appears in advanced coding interviews. This problem requires more than just standard DP; it demands a deep understanding of state optimization.

In this video, I'll walk you through how to tackle this grid-based DP problem, and then introduce the powerful Convex Hull Trick (CHT). Discover how CHT efficiently optimizes certain linear recurrence relations, transforming a naive O(N^2) DP into a blazing fast O(N log N) or O(N) solution. This technique is a game-changer for competitive programming and signals a high level of algorithmic proficiency to companies like Meta.

✅ What you'll learn:
1.  Crafting a precise DP state for complex grid problems.
2.  Recognizing the structure amenable to Convex Hull Trick.
3.  Detailed explanation and geometric intuition behind CHT.
4.  Practical C++ implementation of CHT for dynamic programming.
5.  Why top tech companies value this advanced optimization technique.

