The Dark Matter Mirage: Why the Universe's Missing Mass Is an Even Deeper Mystery,"For decades, dark matter has been the universe's ultimate phantom – an invisible substance making up 27% of all mass, yet defying direct detection. Scientists believed the culprit was a Weakly Interacting Massive Particle (WIMP), a theoretical entity that would finally complete our cosmic inventory. But what if the WIMP hunt is a wild goose chase?

In this video, we delve into the growing scientific unease as groundbreaking experiments like LUX-ZEPLIN continue to yield null results, pushing the boundaries of our understanding to a breaking point. Are we facing a 'dark matter crisis' akin to previous paradigm shifts in physics? We explore radical alternative theories – from Modified Newtonian Dynamics (MOND) suggesting gravity itself behaves differently on cosmic scales, to exotic 'dark' particles like axions, and even the controversial idea of primordial black holes secretly accounting for the universe's missing gravity. Join our 'Cosmic Cartographers' as we map the edges of our knowledge and confront the possibility that the universe's greatest secret is not a particle, but a fundamental misunderstanding of reality itself.

