Dr. Emily Chen | The Science of Sleep: Unlocking Your Best Rest for Health & Longevity | Ep 35,"Sleep is not merely a break from our day; it's a fundamental pillar of health, performance, and longevity, yet it remains one of the most misunderstood and neglected aspects of modern life. With endless conflicting advice, personal anecdotes, and a pervasive 'sleep when you're dead' mentality, cutting through the noise to understand what truly constitutes restorative sleep can be challenging.

In this episode of Science of Self, we sit down with Dr. Emily Chen, a renowned neuroscientist specializing in sleep and circadian rhythms, and author of the acclaimed book ""The Rest Revolution."" Dr. Chen shares her profound insights into the biological necessity of sleep, how it impacts everything from cognitive function and mood to physical recovery and immune health, and what the latest science reveals about optimizing our rest.

We explore why sleep advice often feels contradictory, dissect common myths that undermine healthy sleep habits, and provide actionable, evidence-based strategies to improve your sleep hygiene. The conversation also delves into the intricate relationship between sleep and long-term health, the role of modern technology in both hindering and helping our sleep, and how to navigate a world that often undervalues the power of a good night's rest.

Dr. Chen is celebrated for her ability to translate complex neuroscientific research into clear, practical guidance, empowering individuals to reclaim their sleep and unlock their full potential.

If you're seeking clarity on how to genuinely improve your sleep, understand its critical role in your overall well-being, and make informed choices for a healthier, longer life, this discussion is an essential listen.

 If you found this conversation insightful, subscribe to Science of Self for deep dives with leading experts on human potential, health, and well-being.

