Why AI Lacks Common Sense: Bridging the Gap with Embodied Intelligence,"Title: Why AI Lacks Common Sense: Bridging the Gap with Embodied Intelligence (Aug 2027)Link: http://arxiv.org/abs/2708.09123v1 (Imaginary paper)Date: August 2027Summary:This video explores the persistent challenge of enabling AI systems to exhibit common sense reasoning, a capability effortless for humans and animals. Drawing insights from developmental psychology, embodied cognition, and neurobiology, we propose that the current data-driven, disembodied approach to AI inherently limits its capacity for true understanding and intuition. We introduce a ""Perceptual-Motor Grounding Framework"" that emphasizes the role of physical interaction, sensory experience, and developmental learning stages in building robust, intuitive AI. The discussion covers the conceptual hurdles and outlines an interdisciplinary research agenda to foster truly intelligent, adaptable systems.Key Topics:- Common sense reasoning- Embodied intelligence- Developmental AI- Perceptual-Motor Grounding Framework- Intuitive physics- Social cognition in AI- Affordances and interaction- Neuro-inspired architectures- Data efficiency vs. experiential learningChapters:00:00 - The Elusive Nature of Common Sense AI01:45 - When AI Breaks: Failures of Intuition03:10 - The Problem with Disembodied Data05:05 - Learning from Babies: Developmental AI06:30 - The Power of Perceptual-Motor Grounding08:00 - Embodiment: More Than Just a Robot Body09:40 - Intuitive Physics and Object Permanence11:15 - Social Interaction as a Learning Mechanism12:50 - Bridging Simulation and Reality14:20 - Towards Experiential Learning Architectures15:55 - The Role of Affordances in AI Perception17:30 - Ethical Implications of Embodied AI19:00 - Future Directions: Neuro-Inspired Systems20:45 - Real-World Adaptability and Generalization",Cognitive AI Insights,87
