"The ""Leaf Sheep"" Sea Slug: This Tiny Creature Eats Sunshine! #seaslug #nature #marinelife","Discover the adorable ""leaf sheep"" sea slug, Costasiella kuroshimae, a miniature marvel that looks like a cartoon character come to life! Found in the waters around Japan, Indonesia, and the Philippines, this tiny mollusk (often less than a centimeter long) isn't just cute – it's a solar-powered superstar. Known for its distinctive green, leaf-like cerata, the leaf sheep sea slug has a remarkable ability called kleptoplasty. After eating algae, it incorporates the chloroplasts from the algae into its own body. These chloroplasts continue to photosynthesize, providing the slug with energy, much like a plant. It's essentially a solar-powered animal! Watch as these tiny ""sheep"" graze on algae, showcasing their unique appearance and incredible ability to steal and use the sun's energy. A truly fascinating example of nature's ingenuity in miniature.",Ocean Oddities Uncovered,5
