Seaborn Styling Secrets: Advanced Customization for Impactful Visuals,"Tired of basic Seaborn plots? Learn to transform your data visualizations into professional, impactful insights using advanced customization techniques! Seaborn is incredible for statistical plotting, but to truly tell your data's story and create dashboards that stand out, mastering customization is key. This tutorial will take your Seaborn skills to the next level.

In this tutorial, we will cover:
✔ Beyond default themes: Customizing styles and palettes
✔ Fine-tuning plot elements: Titles, labels, legends, annotations
✔ Integrating Matplotlib for ultimate control: `fig, ax` with Seaborn
✔ Conditional formatting and highlighting key data points
✔ Real-world examples for stunning reports

CODE:
import seaborn as sns
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

df = sns.load_dataset(""tips"")

# Custom palette
custom_palette = [""#FF5733"", ""#33FF57"", ""#3357FF""]
sns.set_palette(custom_palette)

# Create a plot with custom elements
plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))
sns.scatterplot(data=df, x=""total_bill"", y=""tip"", hue=""time"", size=""size"", sizes=(20, 200))

plt.title(""Tip Amount vs. Total Bill by Time of Day"", fontsize=16, fontweight='bold')
plt.xlabel(""Total Bill ($"")
plt.ylabel(""Tip ($"")
plt.legend(title=""Time of Day"", loc='upper left')

# Add an annotation
plt.annotate('Highest Tip', xy=(25, 10), xytext=(30, 11),
             arrowprops=dict(facecolor='black', shrink=0.05),
             fontsize=10, color='red')

plt.grid(True, linestyle='--', alpha=0.6)
plt.tight_layout()
plt.show()

