MSc 2nd Semester Organic Chemistry 2024 Exam Review: Top 25 Short Questions #organicchemistry #chemistry #examprep,"Reaction Mechanisms (PYQ) 1. Explain the SN1 and SN2 reaction mechanisms with suitable examples. 2. Discuss electrophilic aromatic substitution (EAS) with respect to activating and deactivating groups. 3. Derive the mechanism of Michael addition. 4. Explain the factors affecting carbocation stability. 5. What are elimination reactions? Differentiate E1 and E2 pathways. — Spectroscopy (PYQ) 6. Explain the principle of Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (NMR) spectroscopy and its application in structure elucidation. 7. Discuss the different types of stretching and bending vibrations in IR spectroscopy. 8. How is mass spectrometry used to determine molecular weight and fragmentation patterns? 9. Explain chemical shift and coupling constant in 1H NMR. 10. Describe the concept of UV-Vis spectroscopy and Beer-Lambert Law. — Pericyclic Reactions (PYQ) 11. Explain the Woodward-Hoffmann rules for electrocyclic reactions. 12. Discuss the mechanism and applications of the Diels-Alder reaction. 13. What are sigmatropic rearrangements? Give an example. 14. Explain the concept of frontier molecular orbitals (FMO) in pericyclic reactions. 15. Differentiate between thermal and photochemical pericyclic reactions. — Stereochemistry (PYQ) 16. Define chirality, enantiomers, and diastereomers with examples. 17. Explain the Cahn-Ingold-Prelog (CIP) rules for assigning R/S configurations. 18. Discuss the concept of optical isomerism and specific rotation. 19. What is conformational analysis? Explain with respect to cyclohexane. 20. Explain the importance of stereochemistry in drug design.",ChemPulse Academy,95
