What Happens If You Never Yawn?,"What happens if you never yawn?

Yawning is an involuntary action, often linked to tiredness or boredom, but its true purpose is still debated! Some theories suggest it helps regulate brain temperature, increase alertness, or even stretch jaw muscles.

If you somehow stopped yawning, your brain might struggle to regulate its temperature, leading to decreased cognitive function and increased fatigue. You'd likely feel more sleepy and less focused throughout the day, even after a full night's sleep.

This short science animation explores the mysterious reasons behind yawning and what could happen if you didn't do it.

