Rad Power Bikes RadRunner 2 - Front Brake Cable Replacement Guide,"Rad Power Bikes RadRunner 2 - Front Brake Cable Replacement Guide

This video provides a step-by-step tutorial on how to replace the front brake cable on your Rad Power Bikes RadRunner 2 e-bike. Maintain optimal braking performance and ensure your safety by following this detailed repair process.

Tools Required:
5mm Hex Wrench
10mm Wrench
Wire Cutters
Crimping Tool (optional, for cable end cap)

Part 1: Preparation & Old Cable Removal
1. Ensure the bike is powered off and on a stable stand.
2. Locate the front brake lever on the handlebars. Use the 5mm hex wrench to loosen the cable anchor bolt on the brake caliper.
3. Pull the old cable free from the brake lever housing and the caliper.
4. Carefully remove the old cable from all cable guides along the frame.

Part 2: New Cable Installation
1. Insert the barrel end of the new brake cable into the brake lever housing, ensuring it seats correctly.
2. Route the new cable through all existing cable guides on the frame, matching the path of the old cable.
3. Insert the free end of the cable through the cable anchor bolt on the brake caliper.
4. Pull the cable taut to remove slack, then tighten the cable anchor bolt with the 5mm hex wrench, ensuring proper tension (refer to your RadRunner 2 manual for specific torque settings).
5. Test the brake lever action. Adjust cable tension at the caliper and/or the barrel adjuster on the brake lever until the brake engages firmly without rubbing.
6. Cut any excess cable length approximately 1-2 inches past the anchor bolt using wire cutters.
7. Crimp a new cable end cap onto the cut end to prevent fraying (optional but recommended).

Part 3: Final Checks
1. Spin the front wheel to ensure no brake rub occurs when the lever is released.
2. Apply the front brake firmly several times to ensure it engages properly and smoothly.
3. Double-check all bolts for tightness. Your front brake cable replacement is complete!",E-Bike Mechanics Hub,8
