"Smart Speakers, Privacy & Trust - Is Your AI Assistant Listening...to Everything?","What happens when the technology designed to make your life easier becomes an ear to your private world? In this episode, we dive into the pervasive world of smart speakers and AI assistants, asking: What happens to trust when your always-on device starts listening a little too closely, or worse, gets compromised? Drawing upon recent reports of smart device vulnerabilities and potential data misuse, we explore how our digital trust is built, easily shattered, and whether that trust can ever be fully restored once a device designed for convenience puts your privacy at risk. This isn’t just about gadgets. It’s about the unseen boundaries we allow technology to cross, and the implications for our most personal spaces. Expect discussions on ambient intelligence, the economics of data, real-world privacy breaches, and the uncomfortable truth that convenience often comes at a hidden cost. In This Episode, We Discuss: The Intimacy Attack Surface: Why the real vulnerability in ambient AI isn't just the code, it's the personal data it collects. Feature vs. Flaw: Why a privacy 'feature' can feel like a data vulnerability (and why that distinction matters for trust). Transparency After a Breach: Does an AI company admitting a data leak actually rebuild user trust or just make them unplug their devices? The Social Contract of AI: Why you’re not just trusting the device, but the company, their algorithms, and the entire ecosystem feeding on your data. LINKS The Privacy Implications of Smart Home Assistants by Sarah Jones (2023) (https://www.dataprivacyjournal.org/ai-privacy-2023) Understanding User Trust in Conversational AI Systems by Mark Davis & Emily Chen (2022) (https://www.humancenteredai.org/trust-in-ai) Test your privacy awareness with the 'Data Surveillance Quiz' (https://www.digitalrightsfoundation.com/privacy-quiz)",Digital Deciphers - Tech & Society Insights,35
