Unpacking the Brain: How Neuroscience Shapes AI's Neural Networks,"In this insightful talk, Dr. Anya Sharma, a leading researcher in computational neuroscience, demystifies the profound connections between the human brain and artificial intelligence. She explores how the architecture and functioning of biological neural networks have inspired and continue to inform the development of modern AI's neural networks. Dr. Sharma, currently a principal investigator at the Institute for Cognitive Computing and an adjunct professor at the University of Hyperion, brings her multidisciplinary expertise in neuroscience, machine learning, and computational modeling to offer a clear and accessible perspective on AI's biological roots. Moving beyond surface-level comparisons, the lecture delves into key neuroscientific principles such as synaptic plasticity, distributed processing, and hierarchical organization, illustrating their computational analogues in deep learning models. Techniques from neuroanatomy, electrophysiology, and cognitive psychology provide frameworks for understanding how AI learns, adapts, and processes information. The session unpacks how these biological inspirations drive advancements in areas like pattern recognition, sensory processing, and even rudimentary forms of 'reasoning' in AI. This lecture is part of the 'Frontiers in Cognition' series, presented by Cognitive Frontiers, aimed at bridging the gap between cutting-edge scientific research and public understanding. Dr. Sharma's commitment to scientific communication shines through, making complex concepts intelligible without oversimplification. #Neuroscience #ArtificialIntelligence #AI #NeuralNetworks #DeepLearning #ComputationalNeuroscience #BrainScience #CognitiveComputing #MachineLearning #ScienceEducation #CognitiveFrontiers",Cognitive Frontiers,250
