Why Do Onions Make You Cry? 😭 (The Surprising Chemistry!),"Ever wonder why chopping onions brings tears to your eyes? 😭 It's not just you! The secret lies in a fascinating chemical reaction. When you cut an onion, you break open its cells, releasing sulfur compounds. These compounds mix with enzymes, creating a volatile gas called syn-propanethial S-oxide. This gas floats up to your eyes, irritating the nerves and triggering your tear ducts to produce tears to wash it away! So next time you're shedding tears over an onion, remember it's pure science at work! ✨ Subscribe for more intriguing everyday facts! ✨",@CuriousCornerFacts,85
