Is Time an Illusion? Einstein's Biggest Regret & Feynman's Insight,"Is Time an Illusion? Einstein's Biggest Regret & Feynman's Insight

Every second, every minute, every day — we experience time as a relentless forward march. But what if that ticking clock is fundamentally misleading?

In this thought-provoking exploration, we dive into one of physics' deepest mysteries: the true nature of time. From Einstein's revolutionary theories to the mind-bending implications of quantum mechanics, we uncover why many brilliant minds, including Feynman, suggest our perception of time might be a profound illusion.

This video breaks down complex concepts, revealing:

• Why the concept of 'now' is a cosmic riddle
• The Block Universe: a controversial theory where past, present, and future coexist
• How General Relativity challenges our linear understanding of time
• Feynman's intuitive perspective on space-time and its properties
• What quantum physics hints about time's ultimate reality

Most people live their lives bound by the clock. But true insight emerges when we question the very fabric of our reality.

This isn't just about physics…
It's about re-evaluating your most fundamental assumptions about existence.

Watch until the end — and you might never look at a clock the same way again.

