 Become a Machine Learning Engineer in 90 Days (Your Action Plan),"Yes, you can develop real Machine Learning Engineering skills in ~90 days—but only if you focus on the right concepts and practical application. This video provides a simple, actionable roadmap  to kickstart your journey into the world of ML Engineering.

 Month 1 — Foundations & Core Python
Focus on robust programming skills and essential math.
Learn:
• Python fundamentals (advanced data structures, OOP)
• Data Structures & Algorithms (for efficiency)
• Linear Algebra & Calculus (ML prerequisites)
• Probability & Statistics (for understanding models)
Core Python tools:
• NumPy, Pandas (for data manipulation)
• Matplotlib, Seaborn (for data visualization)
Mini projects:
• Implement basic algorithms from scratch
• Data cleaning and exploratory analysis tasks
Goal: Build a strong computational and mathematical base.

 Month 2 — Core Machine Learning & Deep Learning
Now, dive into building predictive models.
Learn:
• Supervised Learning (Regression, Classification)
• Unsupervised Learning (Clustering, Dimensionality Reduction)
• Introduction to Deep Learning (NN basics, CNNs, RNNs)
Use:
• Scikit-learn (for traditional ML)
• TensorFlow or PyTorch (for Deep Learning)
Practice:
• Image classification with CNNs
• Text sentiment analysis with RNNs
• Anomaly detection
Goal: Understand, train, and evaluate various ML and DL models.

 Final Month — Projects, MLOps & Deployment
This stage is crucial for becoming job-ready.
Build 2–3 strong end-to-end projects:
• Develop a recommendation system
• Build a deployed image recognition API
• Create a time series forecasting model
Learn basics of:
• MLOps (version control, CI/CD for ML, monitoring)
• Cloud deployment (AWS Sagemaker, GCP AI Platform, Azure ML)
Publish them on:
• GitHub (with clear documentation)
• Personal portfolio website
Goal: Showcase your ability to build, deploy, and manage ML solutions.

 Daily Routine (Essential for Success)
Dedicate 3–4 hours daily:
• 1 hour learning concepts & theory
• 2 hours coding, debugging, and practice problems
• 1 hour project work & documentation
Consistency is more important than raw speed. Small, daily efforts compound quickly.

⚠️ Reality Check
You won’t become a seasoned ML architect in 3 months. However, this plan can make you:
• A job-ready entry-level ML Engineer
• A strong candidate for ML internships
• Proficient in building and deploying ML models

 Final Advice
Don’t try to learn every algorithm or framework. Focus on:
• Python programming proficiency
• Strong understanding of core ML/DL concepts
• Ability to build and deploy practical projects
• Continuous learning and problem-solving

 Remember:
“The best way to predict the future is to create it, one line of code at a time.”",AI Ascent,35
