3 Steps to Crafting a Perfect Dissertation Research Question (Examples Included!) #PhDLife,"Crafting compelling research questions is often the make-or-break point for your dissertation! If you're feeling lost, this video is for you. We break down the seemingly complex process of formulating perfect research questions into 3 easy-to-follow steps, complete with practical examples to guide you. Step 1: Pinpoint Your Passion & Problem Before you can ask, you need to know *what* you're asking about. We'll show you how to identify a broad area of interest and then zoom in on a specific, unresolved problem or gap in existing literature. Think of it as finding your academic North Star! Step 2: Define Your Scope & Variables Once you have your problem, how do you make it researchable? This step focuses on clearly defining the boundaries of your study and identifying the key concepts or variables you'll be investigating. We'll discuss how to avoid questions that are too broad or too narrow. Step 3: Structure for Clarity & Answerability The final step is all about the wording. Learn to construct questions that are clear, concise, and most importantly, answerable through systematic research. We'll cover different types of research questions (descriptive, exploratory, explanatory) and provide templates you can adapt. Examples include: * Instead of 'How does social media affect people?', try 'To what extent does frequent Instagram use correlate with increased anxiety levels among university students aged 18-22 in urban settings?' * Instead of 'What is leadership?', try 'How do transformational leadership styles impact employee job satisfaction in tech startups in Silicon Valley?' Don't let fuzzy questions derail your research journey! Master this skill early, and your entire dissertation will thank you. If this guide helped you gain clarity, hit the like button and subscribe to Academic Edge for more essential dissertation and thesis tips! #dissertation #researchquestions #phdlife #academicsuccess #thesistips #gradstudent",Academic Edge,135
