Photosynthesis Decoded | Light-Dependent & Light-Independent Reactions Explained,"This video delves deep into the intricate process of photosynthesis, the foundation of almost all life on Earth. We'll start by breaking down the light-dependent reactions, explaining how chlorophyll captures light energy to produce ATP and NADPH. Discover the role of photosystems I and II, the electron transport chain, and chemiosmosis in converting light into chemical energy. Following this, we'll explore the light-independent reactions, commonly known as the Calvin Cycle. Learn how CO2 is fixed, reduced, and regenerated to synthesize glucose. This lecture will also touch upon factors affecting photosynthesis rates and adaptations in different plant types (C3, C4, CAM). Perfect for high school biology, college-level introductory biology, NEET, and competitive exam preparation, this video aims to provide a comprehensive and clear understanding of how plants make their food.",BioBytes Lab,65
LMS 'Duchess of Sutherland' Conquers Ais Gill Unassisted With 12 Coaches at 45mph!,"Following an incredible summer of steam, we bring you one of the most anticipated runs of the year: LMS Princess Coronation Class No. 6233 'Duchess of Sutherland' tackling the legendary Settle-Carlisle line's formidable Ais Gill summit. This time, the magnificent Duchess was tasked with an impressive 12-coach load, and critically, entirely unassisted. Our on-board timers recorded a minimum speed of 45mph over the summit, a testament to her raw power and the skill of the crew, making it one of the most powerful unassisted ascents in recent preservation history. While not a speed record, the sheer challenge of hauling such a load up the steepest main line incline in England without pilot assistance is truly awe-inspiring. This special run, organized by The Railway Touring Company, once again showcased the enduring might of British steam and its dedicated following. The footage captures her majesty at various iconic points, including a stunning climb past Ribblehead Viaduct, a powerful assault on the higher slopes near Dent, and her final triumph near the summit of Ais Gill. Witnessing such pure steam power is a rare and thrilling experience for any enthusiast. We hope you enjoy this epic display of steam locomotive engineering! #steamtrain #trains #railways #duchessofsutherland #settlecarlisle #steamlocomotive #heritage #trainspotting #britishrailways",Iron Horse Chronicles,8123
