Deconstructing Intentionality: A Phenomenological Approach to AI Agency,"This presentation delves into the complex concept of intentionality as it applies to advanced Artificial Intelligence systems. Drawing upon phenomenological philosophy, we explore whether AI can possess genuine 'aboutness' or 'for-ness' in its actions, moving beyond mere computational mimicry. The discussion critically examines frameworks for attributing agency to AI, considering implications for ethical responsibility, legal personhood, and the very definition of consciousness in artificial constructs. We argue that a rigorous phenomenological lens is crucial for understanding the qualitative experience and moral standing of future AI, challenging reductionist views and paving the way for more nuanced human-AI interactions. Key insights will be drawn from Husserl, Heidegger, and Merleau-Ponty, reinterpreted within the context of contemporary AI research and design.",Aletheia AI,2
