Beyond Neurons: Glia Cells' Hidden Influence on Your Thoughts,"For decades, neuroscience focused almost exclusively on neurons as the sole architects of thought and memory. But groundbreaking new research is challenging this neuron-centric view, revealing an astonishing secret: glia cells, once thought to be mere support structures, are actively shaping our cognitive processes.

This video dives deep into the emerging understanding of glial cells – astrocytes, oligodendrocytes, and microglia – and their dynamic roles. Discover how astrocytes form intricate networks that regulate synaptic strength and plasticity, directly impacting learning and memory formation. Learn about oligodendrocytes’ unexpected ability to modulate neural circuit activity beyond myelination, influencing signal speed and brain rhythm. And explore how microglia, the brain's immune cells, actively prune synapses and respond to brain activity, fundamentally affecting development and disease.

This paradigm shift not only redefines our understanding of the brain's computational power but also opens revolutionary avenues for treating neurodegenerative diseases, mental health disorders, and improving cognitive function.

 Reference & Credit: Imaginary Institute of Neuroplasticity, Dr. Elena Petrova
