Wild Nettle Elixir: Traditional Fermented Immune Boost | #wildforaging #nettle #fermentation #naturalremedies,"In this video, I'll share an ancient recipe for boosting your immune system: a fermented elixir made from fresh wild nettles. I collected young nettle tops from a pristine natural spot, washed them thoroughly, and then roughly chopped them. These I place into a large glass jar. To this, I add about 50g of brown sugar (or honey) as a fermentation starter, and a slice of organic lemon for flavor and additional fermentation aid. A few raisins can also help kickstart the process. The mixture is then filled with filtered water, ensuring the nettles are fully submerged. The jar is covered with a cloth and left to ferment in a warm, dark place. After approximately 5-7 days, the elixir will be ready – sparkling and rich in beneficial enzymes and vitamins. I'll show the final result in a follow-up video. If you're interested in wild plants, traditional recipes, and the art of fermentation, subscribe to our channel for more inspiring videos from nature!",Forest Apothecary,2200
