The Man Who Knew Continents Drifted... But Everyone Laughed!,"Imagine discovering that entire continents were slowly drifting across the Earth… and having the entire scientific community laugh at your 'crazy' idea. That's exactly what happened to Alfred Wegener.In the early 20th century, meteorologist Alfred Wegener proposed the groundbreaking theory of continental drift, suggesting that continents were once joined and had slowly moved apart over millions of years. His evidence was compelling – matching coastlines, fossil records, and geological formations across oceans. Yet, his ideas were met with widespread scorn and ridicule for decades.It wasn't until much later, with advancements in oceanography and geophysics, that his fundamental insight was vindicated by the theory of plate tectonics. He went from being a laughingstock… to the visionary who laid the foundation for modern geology.Have you ever had a big idea that people initially dismissed? Share your story in the comments!",Mind Spark Discoveries,821
