"Proofing Demystified: How to Know When Your Dough is PERFECTLY Ready (Science, Not Vibes!)","Are you constantly guessing if your dough is ready for the oven? Over-proofed, under-proofed — it's one of the most frustrating parts of baking, whether you're making sourdough, pizza, or yeasted bread. But what if I told you there's a science to it, not just a 'poke test' and a prayer?

In this video, we're breaking down the exact signs, science, and practical tips to ensure your dough is always perfectly proofed. We'll cover:
• What 'proofing' actually IS: It's more than just waiting for bubbles!
• The role of yeast and gluten: Understanding the magic happening inside your bowl.
• Visual cues vs. the 'poke test': What to look for and what those indentations really mean.
• Temperature and time: How to control these variables for consistent results.
• The consequences: What happens when your dough is under-proofed (dense crumb!) vs. over-proofed (flat, gummy bread!).

Just like with a sourdough starter, understanding the science of proofing removes guesswork and helps you learn. If every loaf comes out differently, it's hard to improve. By learning to recognize the 'peak' of your dough's proof, you can tweak one variable at a time and truly master your baking.

Stop feeling like you're 'doing it wrong' and start baking with confidence. This isn't about rigid rules, but about understanding the principles so you can adapt and get the bread you truly want. Save this if you're struggling with proofing! Comment your biggest proofing woes! Follow for baking science explained like a normal human with a life.

