P-adic Numbers: A Topological Dive into Arithmetic,"Recorded on October 25th, 2027

Speaker: Dr. Anya Sharma (MIT)

Title: P-adic Numbers: A Topological Dive into Arithmetic

Abstract: This talk introduces the fascinating world of p-adic numbers, an alternative way to complete the rational numbers that offers a radically different perspective compared to the familiar real numbers. We will explore their unique topological structure, often described as 'ultrametric' and 'totally disconnected', and how these properties lead to counter-intuitive yet profound insights into number theory.

We will discuss how p-adic valuations give rise to a non-Archimedean metric and the implications for concepts like convergence and continuity. The presentation will highlight applications in number theory, algebraic geometry, and even theoretical physics, demonstrating how these exotic number systems provide a powerful magnifying glass for examining arithmetic properties of integers and rational numbers. The goal is to illuminate how a shift in topological perspective can unlock deep connections within mathematics.",Abstract Math Explorations,55
