Serpent Mound's Celestial Secrets: Unpacking Indigenous Astronomy & Earth Spirituality (Part 1),"On March 12th, 2024, at a public lecture series in Cincinnati, Ohio, **Dr. Elena Ramirez** delivered an insightful presentation on the Great Serpent Mound — one of North America's most remarkable and enigmatic ancient effigy mounds.

In Part 1, Dr. Ramirez introduces the monumental Serpent Mound and begins to unravel its profound connections to Indigenous astronomy, cyclical understandings of time, and the deep reverence for the earth. This segment lays the groundwork for comprehending how ancient earthworks in North America embody sophisticated cosmological knowledge and spiritual practices linked to the land and celestial movements.

The Serpent Mound is far more than a prehistoric earthwork; it represents a powerful visual and spatial narrative embedded in Native American spiritual traditions, reflecting a complex understanding of the cosmos.

Recorded by Ancient Echoes Keepers

—

We are not official representatives or sponsors of Dr. Ramirez's work, but passionate admirers. It was an honor to attend this lecture, and we felt compelled to help amplify the knowledge being shared and the ongoing efforts to preserve these sacred sites.

