Forever Chemicals: Is Your Non-Stick Pan Poisoning You?,"You might love the convenience of your non-stick cookware, but what if it's slowly releasing harmful 'forever chemicals' into your food? PFAS (Per- and Polyfluoroalkyl Substances) are a group of synthetic chemicals found in many everyday products, including non-stick pans, food packaging, and waterproof clothing. They're called 'forever chemicals' because they don't break down easily in the environment or in our bodies. In this video, we delve into the alarming truth about PFAS in your kitchen. How do these chemicals get into our food? What are the documented health risks associated with PFAS exposure, from thyroid issues to certain cancers? And, crucially, what safer alternatives exist for cooking, and how can you minimize your exposure to these persistent toxins? Join us to uncover the hidden dangers lurking in your kitchen and learn how to protect yourself and your family.",EcoInsights Hub,95
