#AISimplified - Activation Functions in 60 Seconds | Deep Learning Basics,"What are activation functions in neural networks?

Activation functions introduce non-linearity into the network, allowing it to learn complex patterns and make sophisticated decisions that go beyond simple linear relationships.

Common examples include:
• ReLU (Rectified Linear Unit)
• Sigmoid
• Tanh (Hyperbolic Tangent)

They determine whether a neuron should be activated or not, processing the output of a neuron before passing it to the next layer.

Next in the series: Backpropagation — how neural networks learn from errors.

