"UTI During Pregnancy: Symptoms, Risks & Safe Treatment for Expecting Moms","Experiencing a Urinary Tract Infection (UTI) while pregnant? You're not alone! UTIs are common during pregnancy, but knowing what to look for and how to treat them safely is crucial for both you and your baby. What are the symptoms of a UTI in pregnancy? Frequent urge to urinate, burning sensation when urinating, cloudy or strong-smelling urine, pelvic discomfort or pain. Why is treatment important? Untreated UTIs can lead to more serious kidney infections, preterm labor, or low birth weight. Always consult your doctor! Antibiotics are often prescribed, and your doctor will choose one that's safe for pregnancy. Prevention Tips: Drink plenty of water, practice good hygiene, don't hold your urine. Watch this video to understand everything you need to know about managing UTIs during your pregnancy journey!",Mama's Medical Guide,1750
