Deploying Infrastructure as Code is only half the battle; maintaining its integrity against manual interventions, out-of-band changes, or unexpected cloud provider updates is critical. Drift can lead to security vulnerabilities, compliance issues, and unpredictable system behavior. We break down the absolute best practices for identifying drift, enforcing desired states, and integrating detection into your automated workflows.

⏱️ Chapters:
0:00 ⚠️ The Hidden Dangers of IaC Drift
0:55  What is Configuration Drift and Why it Matters
1:40  Security & Compliance Risks of Drift
2:25  Automated Drift Detection in CI/CD
3:10  Real-time Monitoring vs. Scheduled Scans
3:50 ️ Tool 1: Driftctl (Open-source Drift Detection)
4:20  Tool 2: Cloud-native Solutions (e.g., AWS Config Rules)
4:55 ⏩ Tool 3: Policy-as-Code for Prevention (e.g., OPA)
5:30 ️ Best Practices for Remediation & Alerting

