The Nanoscale Challenge: Designing Perovskite Catalysts for Efficient CO2 Reduction,"Contributors:
    • Prof. Elena Petrova
    • Dr. Kenji Tanaka

Thanks for considering to support the show on buymeacoffee.com/catalysisfrontiers ☕ 

In this episode of Catalysis Frontiers, I spoke with Prof. Elena Petrova, a leading expert in solid-state chemistry and electrocatalysis at the Technical University of Berlin, and Dr. Kenji Tanaka, a materials scientist specializing in advanced characterization techniques. We delve into the critical need for efficient CO2 reduction technologies and the promising role of perovskite materials in achieving this. We explore the structural intricacies of perovskites, their tunable properties, and the quantum mechanical challenges in optimizing their catalytic activity for converting CO2 into valuable chemicals like syngas or methanol. Prof. Petrova shares insights from her latest research on defect engineering in metal-organic framework (MOF) templated perovskites, aiming to enhance selectivity and durability under industrial conditions. Dr. Tanaka discusses the use of in-situ spectroscopy and density functional theory (DFT) simulations to understand reaction mechanisms at the atomic scale. The conversation addresses the current limitations of noble metal catalysts and the economic imperative to develop earth-abundant, high-performance alternatives. We conclude by discussing the future outlook for large-scale CO2 utilization and the interdisciplinary efforts required to bring these advanced catalytic systems from laboratory to industrial application.

• 00:00 – Introduction to CO2 Reduction and Perovskites
• 08:45 – Structural Design and Tunability of Perovskite Catalysts
• 16:30 – Defect Engineering for Enhanced Selectivity

• 24:10 – In-situ Characterization and DFT Simulations
• 32:05 – Economic Challenges and Future Outlook for CO2 Utilization

More to read on the topic including the discussed publications:
• E. Petrova, K. Tanaka, ""Defect Engineering in Perovskite Oxides for CO2 Electrocatalysis,"" ACS Catal. 2024, 14, 12345–12356. https://doi.org/10.1021/acscatal.4c01234
• K. Tanaka, E. Petrova, ""In-situ Spectroscopic Probes of CO2 Reduction on Perovskite Surfaces,"" J. Mater. Chem. A 2023, 11, 7890–7901. https://doi.org/10.1039/D3TA07890G
• L. Zhang, X. Wang, ""Recent Advances in Perovskite-based Catalysts for CO2 Conversion,"" Chem. Soc. Rev. 2022, 51, 4567–4589. https://doi.org/10.1039/D2CS04567Z

More about Prof. Petrova's group:
• Homepage: https://www.uni-berlin.de/petrova-group
• ResearchGate: https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Elena-Petrova

