Meiosis | Cell Cycle and Cell Division | NEET 2026 | Biology Class 11

Mastering Meiosis is a cornerstone for excelling in Plant Reproduction and Genetics for NEET 2026. In this lecture, we delve deep into the intricate process of Cell Division - Meiosis, explaining its stages and significance in a clear, conceptual, and exam-oriented manner. This topic is directly aligned with NCERT Biology Class 11, making it indispensable for NEET aspirants and those preparing for board exams.

In this session, you will learn the different phases of Meiosis I (Prophase I, Metaphase I, Anaphase I, Telophase I) and Meiosis II, focusing on key events like crossing over and reductional division. We'll provide clear diagrams, easy-to-understand explanations, and common pitfalls to avoid, along with tricks to remember the sequence and significance for the exam. This video is ideal for NEET 2026 preparation, board exams, and building a strong foundation in cell biology.

If you aim to master NCERT Biology line-by-line and boost your NEET score, ensure you watch the full video and regularly revise these crucial concepts.

🔬 Topics Covered:
• Introduction to Meiosis
• Meiosis I: Prophase I (Leptotene, Zygotene, Pachytene, Diplotene, Diakinesis), Metaphase I, Anaphase I, Telophase I
• Meiosis II: Prophase II, Metaphase II, Anaphase II, Telophase II
• Significance of Meiosis (Genetic variation, Gamete formation)
• Differences between Mitosis and Meiosis
