The ULTIMATE Finish: McLaren 720S | 3-Stage Paint Correction & Gyeon Mohs Coating,"Welcome back, detailing enthusiasts! Today, we're tackling one of the most stunning machines on the road: a beautiful McLaren 720S. This isn't just any detail; we're performing a comprehensive 3-stage paint correction to achieve an absolutely flawless, show-car finish, followed by the application of Gyeon Mohs ceramic coating for unparalleled protection and gloss.
The car arrived with typical swirl marks and minor imperfections from daily driving, but our goal was perfection. We started with a thorough decontamination wash, including iron and tar removal, followed by a careful clay bar treatment to ensure a perfectly clean surface. Each panel was meticulously inspected under various lighting conditions to identify every single imperfection.
The paint correction involved a multi-stage process:
1.  **Heavy Compounding**: Using cutting-edge compounds and pads to remove deeper scratches and oxidation.
2.  **Refining Polish**: A secondary polish to eliminate any hazing from the compounding stage and bring out incredible clarity.
3.  **Finishing Polish**: A final, ultra-fine polish to maximize gloss and achieve a swirl-free, mirror-like finish.
After achieving paint perfection, we prepped the surface with an IPA wipe-down to ensure maximum bonding for the ceramic coating. We then applied two layers of Gyeon Mohs ceramic coating to the paint, followed by Gyeon Rim for the wheels (removed for full access), and Gyeon View for the glass. The transformation is absolutely mind-blowing!
This video will walk you through every step of this intricate process, showcasing the techniques, tools, and products used to achieve this elite level of finish. If you're passionate about car care and paint perfection, you won't want to miss this!

