Sound Activated LED! 🔊 Clap ON/OFF Light Circuit! #Shorts,"⚡ Sound Activated LED Circuit — Fully Explained!

This circuit automatically turns an LED ON/OFF with sound (e.g., a clap) — completely hands-free! 👏✨

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
💡 COMPONENTS USED:
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
• Electret Condenser Microphone — Detects sound waves
• Op-Amp (e.g., LM358) — Amplifies and compares sound signal
• Transistor (e.g., BC547) — Switches the LED
• Current Limiting Resistor — Protects LED
• LED Indicator — Visual Output
• Potentiometer — Sensitivity Adjustment
• Power Input (VCC) — 5V Supply

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
⚙️ HOW IT WORKS:
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
🗣️ Sound Waves Hit Microphone
→ Microphone converts sound to electrical signal
→ Op-Amp amplifies signal and compares to a set threshold
→ If sound is loud enough (e.g., a clap),
→ Op-Amp output triggers the Transistor
→ Transistor turns the LED ON or OFF! (Toggle action possible with slight modification)

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
