AI-Powered Data Quality & Anomaly Detection for E-commerce | Python • Airflow • BigQuery • OpenAI,"Business Context: E-commerce businesses rely heavily on accurate sales and operational data for decision-making. However, data quality issues, such as missing values, outliers, or erroneous entries, can lead to flawed insights and financial losses. Manual data validation is often reactive, time-consuming, and prone to human error.

The AnomalyGuard Project demonstrates an automated data quality framework designed for e-commerce. This system proactively identifies and flags data anomalies and potential quality issues within sales datasets, leveraging AI to provide contextual explanations and streamline data governance.

Impact:
Built an end-to-end automated data pipeline for continuous data quality monitoring in e-commerce.
Implemented intelligent anomaly detection using machine learning, significantly reducing manual effort and improving data reliability.
Enabled AI-assisted root cause analysis, where an AI agent provides insights into potential reasons for detected anomalies.
Delivered a real-time dashboard for data stewards to review, validate, and manage flagged anomalies.
Established an audit trail for all AI-detected issues and subsequent human interventions, ensuring transparency and continuous model improvement.

Data Stack:

Data Ingestion & Storage
Google BigQuery (scalable data warehousing for e-commerce sales data)

Workflow Orchestration
Apache Airflow (scheduling and managing data quality pipelines)

Data Processing & Anomaly Detection
Python (Pandas for data manipulation, Scikit-learn for anomaly detection algorithms like Isolation Forest or DBSCAN)

AI Integration
OpenAI API (for generating contextual explanations and potential root causes for anomalies)

Reporting & Alerting
Streamlit (interactive dashboard for data anomaly review)
Discord Webhooks (real-time alerts for critical anomalies)

Version Control
GitHub",Automated Insights Lab,78
