Pharmacokinetics vs Pharmacodynamics | MedSci Mentor,"Pharmacokinetics (PK) and Pharmacodynamics (PD) are two critical branches of pharmacology that describe how drugs interact with the body. Pharmacokinetics deals with the ""what the body does to the drug"" – absorption, distribution, metabolism, and excretion (ADME). Pharmacodynamics, on the other hand, focuses on ""what the drug does to the body"" – the biochemical, physiological, and molecular effects of drugs, including their mechanism of action. Understanding the distinction between PK and PD is essential for rational drug design, dosing regimens, and predicting therapeutic outcomes and potential side effects. This video simplifies these complex concepts for students and professionals alike. #Pharmacokinetics #Pharmacodynamics #Pharmacology #DrugAction #ADME #DrugMetabolism #PharmaceuticalScience #MedicalEducation #PharmacyStudents #ScienceExplained #DrugDevelopment #ClinicalPharmacology #StudyTips #Biochemistry #HealthSciences #Education #Learning #PharmacologyNotes #ScienceEducation #YouTubeEducation #PharmaConcepts #MedicalStudents #StudyPharmacy",MedSci Mentor,75
