Interpretable AI: Beyond Performance - Understanding LLM Decision Paths with Explainable Methods,"Talk Title: Interpretable AI: Beyond Performance - Understanding LLM Decision Paths with Explainable Methods. Abstract: As large language models become ubiquitous, understanding their internal decision-making processes, rather than just their output performance, is crucial for trust and safety. This talk explores novel methodologies for extracting interpretable insights from LLMs, even when direct model access is restricted. We present techniques for post-hoc explanation generation, causal inference in black-box models, and the use of simplified surrogate models to approximate complex LLM behaviors. Our findings demonstrate that meaningful interpretability can be achieved with carefully designed probes and analysis frameworks, offering pathways to diagnose biases, identify failure modes, and enhance the reliability of AI systems without requiring full model transparency. This research aims to bridge the gap between high-performing black-box LLMs and the growing demand for explainable AI.",AI Ethics & Interpretability Research,25
