AI in the Courts: When Algorithms Decide Justice,"What happens when Artificial Intelligence starts making decisions in the courtroom?This video dives into the escalating debate surrounding the use of AI in judicial systems, from predictive policing to sentencing algorithms. We uncover the ethical quagmire of algorithmic bias, the potential erosion of due process, and what it means for the very concept of justice.As AI models are increasingly deployed to assist judges and legal professionals, fundamental questions arise: Can an algorithm truly be fair? Who is accountable when AI makes a wrong decision? Is this a step towards a more efficient legal system or a dangerous path to automated injustice?We examine real-world cases, explore the legal challenges, and discuss the global push for AI regulation in the justice sector. This analysis delves into the societal, ethical, and legal implications of integrating AI into the foundations of our legal systems, and what it means for the future of human rights and justice worldwide.Topics Covered• AI in the judiciary• Algorithmic bias in legal decisions• Predictive policing ethics• Due process and AI• Future of human judges• AI governance in legal systems",Legal Tech Frontiers,195
