s #DIYGardening #HouseplantCare #GrowYourOwn #GardeningForBeginners #FreePlants #RootingCuttings",GreenThumb Gurus,1250
I made a homemade #oatmealcremepie better than #littledebbie! #copycatrecipe #baking,"Remember those soft, chewy oatmeal cookies with that creamy filling in the middle? Little Debbie Oatmeal Creme Pies were a lunchbox staple!

I've spent weeks perfecting a homemade version that captures all that nostalgic comfort, but with even richer flavors and a melt-in-your-mouth texture you won't believe.

Seriously, once you try these, you'll never go back to the store-bought kind. They're that good.

Save this recipe and treat yourself to a taste of childhood, elevated!

**Homemade Oatmeal Creme Pies Copycat**

**Cookies:**
1 cup (2 sticks) unsalted butter, softened
1 cup packed light brown sugar
½ cup granulated sugar
2 large eggs
1 tsp vanilla extract
1 ½ cups all-purpose flour
1 tsp baking soda
½ tsp salt
1 tsp ground cinnamon
¼ tsp ground nutmeg
3 cups old-fashioned rolled oats

**Cream Filling:**
½ cup (1 stick) unsalted butter, softened
1 cup powdered sugar
1 tsp vanilla extract
2 tbsp heavy cream or milk

**How to Make:**
1. Preheat oven to 375°F (190°C). Line baking sheets with parchment paper.
2. In a large bowl, cream together softened butter, brown sugar, and granulated sugar until light and fluffy.
3. Beat in eggs one at a time, then stir in vanilla.
4. In a separate bowl, whisk together flour, baking soda, salt, cinnamon, and nutmeg. Gradually add dry ingredients to the wet ingredients, mixing until just combined.
5. Stir in the rolled oats.
6. Drop rounded tablespoons of dough onto prepared baking sheets, about 2 inches apart.
7. Bake for 8-10 minutes, or until edges are golden brown and centers are set. Let cool on the baking sheets for a few minutes before transferring to a wire rack to cool completely.

**For the Cream Filling:**
1. In a medium bowl, beat softened butter until creamy.
2. Gradually add powdered sugar, beating until smooth.
3. Stir in vanilla extract and heavy cream, beating until light and fluffy.

**Assemble:**
1. Once cookies are completely cool, spread a generous amount of cream filling on the flat side of one cookie. Top with another cookie, pressing gently to create a sandwich.
2. Repeat with remaining cookies and filling.
3. Store in an airtight container at room temperature for up to 3 days, or refrigerate for longer freshness.

