 MongoDB Replica Set Setup on Ubuntu 24.04 | Step-by-Step High Availability Guide ⚡ #mongodb #replicaset," Complete beginner-friendly, step-by-step guide to set up a MongoDB Replica Set on Ubuntu 24.04 LTS. Learn how to install, configure, initiate, and test for high availability.

#  What is MongoDB?
MongoDB is an open-source, NoSQL document database that provides high performance, high availability, and easy scalability.

#  1. What is a MongoDB Replica Set?
A Replica Set in MongoDB is a group of mongod processes that maintain the same data set. It provides redundancy and high availability. One member is deemed the primary, and the others are secondaries.

## ✅ Why we use it
*  High Availability → automatic failover if the primary node fails.
* ⚡ Read Scalability → distribute read operations across secondary nodes.
*  Data Redundancy → protection against data loss due to hardware failures.

# ️ 2. Architecture
PRIMARY (192.168.1.101)
        ↓
   Replication
        ↓
SECONDARY (192.168.1.102)
        ↓
   Replication
        ↓
SECONDARY (192.168.1.103)

# ️ 3. Server Details
+ ----------- + ----------------- +
| Role        | IP                |
+ ----------- + ----------------- +
| Primary     | 192.168.1.101     |
| Secondary   | 192.168.1.102     |
| Secondary   | 192.168.1.103     |
+ ----------- + ----------------- +

#  USE CASE IN REAL WORLD
* E-commerce platforms requiring constant uptime.
* Content Management Systems (CMS) with high read loads.
* IoT data ingestion systems requiring data resilience.

#  YOU ARE NOW DONE
You now know:
* ✅ MongoDB Installation on Ubuntu 24.04
* ✅ Replica Set Configuration
* ✅ Initiating a Replica Set
* ✅ Testing Failover and Redundancy

