Building Real-time Data Quality Pipelines with Apache Flink & Deequ,"Ensuring data quality in high-throughput streaming environments is a critical challenge for modern data teams. Data arriving late, incomplete, or corrupted can lead to flawed analytics and poor business decisions. This video provides a technical deep dive into how Apache Flink, a powerful stream processing framework, can be combined with Deequ, a library for defining and testing data quality, to build robust real-time data quality pipelines.

We will walk through a practical implementation, demonstrating how to move from reactive data validation to proactive, continuous quality assurance directly within your data streams.

Technical Deep Dive
We cover the integration of Flink and Deequ across key aspects of real-time data processing:

Stream Ingestion (Apache Kafka): Setting up Flink to consume data from Kafka topics.

Quality Definition (Deequ): Programmatically defining data quality constraints such as completeness, uniqueness, data type conformance, and custom metrics.

Real-time Processing (Apache Flink): Implementing Flink jobs to apply Deequ checks on streaming data in real-time.

Alerting & Monitoring: Integrating with external systems (e.g., Prometheus, Grafana) for visualizing quality metrics and triggering alerts on anomalies.

Key Demo Moments
Flink Job Setup: Deploying a Flink streaming application with Deequ checks.

Constraint Definition: Writing Deequ constraints for a sample streaming dataset.

Anomaly Detection: Demonstrating how real-time data quality checks identify and report anomalies.

Alerting Workflow: Visualizing quality metrics and triggering an alert when a defined threshold is breached.


