Advanced Grid-Tied Solar Inverter Design & MPPT Control in Simulink,"Implementation Plan:
---------------------------

Step 1: Construct a detailed PV array model, coupled with a DC-DC boost converter for voltage regulation and Maximum Power Point Tracking (MPPT) using a Perturb and Observe algorithm in Simulink.

Step 2: Design and implement a three-phase voltage source inverter (VSI) for converting DC power from the PV array to AC power suitable for grid synchronization.

Step 3: Develop advanced current and voltage control loops for the inverter, ensuring stable grid connection, power factor control, and harmonic reduction under varying grid conditions.

Step 4: Simulate the entire grid-tied solar inverter system under dynamic scenarios, including fluctuating solar irradiance, temperature changes, and grid disturbances.

Step 5: Analyze the system's performance metrics, focusing on power transfer efficiency, grid current harmonics (THD), MPPT tracking accuracy, and DC-link voltage stability.

Step 6: Generate comprehensive plots for key performance indicators:
 6.1 : Time vs PV Array Power (W)
 6.2 : Time vs Grid Power (W)
 6.3 : Time vs Grid Voltage (V) and Current (A)
 6.4 : Time vs MPPT Efficiency (%)
 6.5 : THD Analysis of Grid Current

Software Requirements:
-----------------------------
 1. Development Tool: Matlab-R2023a/Simulink or above
 2. Operating System: Windows 10 (64-bit) or above

