The Sentinel Array: 3 Top Deep-Sky Cameras Compared Side-by-Side!,"Welcome to the Sentinel Array, my custom-built triple-camera astrophotography rig designed for one purpose: to determine which of three leading deep-sky cameras truly excels in different scenarios. In this video, I put three of the most popular cooled CMOS cameras head-to-head, capturing the same targets at the same time, under the same conditions.

I'm comparing:
*   ZWO ASI2600MC Pro: The large-sensor, one-shot color powerhouse.
*   ZWO ASI533MC Pro: The innovative square-sensor, one-shot color camera with zero amp glow.
*   ZWO ASI2600MM Pro: The monochrome version of the 2600, ideal for narrowband imaging.

Join me as I detail the construction of the Sentinel Array – how I mounted three identical small aperture refractors (e.g., RedCat 51s or similar) on a single equatorial mount, managed power and data, and ensured precise alignment for simultaneous capture. I'll walk through my control system setup and demonstrate the imaging process.

Then, we'll dive deep into the data! I'll perform a pixel-by-pixel analysis of raw frames and stacked images, comparing:
*   Field of View: How sensor size impacts your framing.
*   Noise Performance: Differences across sensors and camera types.
*   Sensitivity & Quantum Efficiency: Real-world impact on faint detail.
*   Color Rendition (OSC): How the MC cameras handle natural colors.
*   Narrowband Potential (Mono): The power of filters with the MM camera.
*   Star Handling: Comparing star sizes and characteristics.
*   Processing Workflow: The effort required for each camera type.

I'll share my insights on the strengths and weaknesses of each camera, and ultimately help you decide which one is the best fit for your astrophotography journey. Whether you're considering your first dedicated astro camera or looking to upgrade, this comparison is for you!

