"Sediment Transport Mechanics (Part 1) | Shields Parameter, Critical Shear Stress & Bedforms","Building upon the fundamental concepts of fluid flow, this video delves into Sediment Transport Mechanics (Part 1) — a pivotal topic for Sedimentology, Fluvial Geomorphology, Oceanography, and Civil Engineering.

We explore the forces that move sediment, including:

✔️ Fluid Shear Stress (the driving force)
✔️ Critical Shear Stress (threshold for movement)
✔️ Shields Parameter (dimensionless criterion for sediment motion)
✔️ Modes of Sediment Transport (bedload vs. suspended load)
✔️ Introduction to Bedforms (ripples, dunes, bars) and their formation

These advanced concepts are extremely important for competitive exams like IIT JAM, CUET PG, GATE Geology, and are integral to B.Sc and M.Sc Earth Sciences curricula.

📚 What you will learn:

✅ How fluid shear stress is calculated and its role in erosion
✅ The concept of critical shear stress and the Shields diagram
✅ Differentiating between bedload and suspended load transport
✅ The controls on the formation and migration of various bedforms

🎯 Perfect for:

B.Sc / M.Sc Geology & Earth Science students

Environmental Science students focusing on aquatic systems

Civil Engineering students specializing in hydraulics and river management

IIT JAM, CUET PG, and GATE Geology aspirants

✨ Don’t forget to:

Like 👍 | Share ➡️ | Subscribe 🔔 for more in-depth Earth Science lectures!",GeoFormations Lab,68
