Sankey Diagram Explained | Visualizing Flow and Relationships ☀️ #datascience #datavisualization #flowanalysis,"What is a Sankey Diagram?

A Sankey diagram is a type of flow diagram that illustrates the flow of a quantity (such as energy, materials, or money) from one set of values to another. They are characterized by their varying widths, which are drawn proportionally to the flow quantity they represent.

Unlike traditional bar or line charts, Sankey diagrams excel at showing the distribution and transitions of quantities across different stages or categories.

In this reel, you’ll learn:
• What a Sankey diagram is
• How it visualizes complex flows
• Why the 'width' of the lines matters
• How it helps in understanding resource allocation and movement

Example uses:
• Energy consumption breakdowns
• Website user journeys
• Supply chain logistics

Key insight:
The paths and their varying thicknesses reveal the major contributors and the magnitude of transfers, highlighting bottlenecks or significant flows.

Follow for more concise data visualization explanations and insights.

#SankeyDiagram #DataVisualization #FlowAnalysis #Analytics #DataScience #InformationDesign",DataVizDojo,112
