The Cat Who Woke Her Owners Moments Before Fire Engulfed Their Home,"Could your pet save your life? This is the extraordinary story of Luna, a rescue cat who became an unexpected hero.

One terrifying night, a family was asleep in their beds when Luna, normally a quiet sleeper, began acting erratically. She clawed at her owner's bedroom door, meowing incessantly with a sound they had never heard before.

Thinking she just wanted attention, they tried to shoo her away. But Luna wouldn't stop. She jumped on the bed, batting at their faces until they finally got up.

As soon as they opened their bedroom door, a thick smell of smoke hit them. Flames were already visible in the kitchen. Luna’s frantic warnings had given them just enough time to evacuate the house with seconds to spare, escaping the blaze unharmed.

Experts believe animals, especially cats, can detect smoke and the scent of fire long before humans can, thanks to their incredibly sensitive noses and ears. Luna wasn't just a beloved pet; she was a guardian angel.

