Dark Energy: The Universe's Accelerating Mystery 💥 #shorts,"The universe isn't just expanding, it's speeding up! But what's pushing it? Scientists call it dark energy – a mysterious, invisible force that's responsible for the accelerated expansion of the cosmos. It's thought to make up about 68% of the universe, acting as a kind of anti-gravity. We know it's there because of observations of distant supernovae, showing the universe expanding faster over time. Dark energy is the driving force behind the universe's ultimate fate. --- ✨ Image Credits: • Supernova Remnant - NASA, ESA, and the Hubble Heritage Team (STScI/AURA) • Cosmic Microwave Background - ESA/Planck Collaboration 🎤 Voice: Liam (en-GB-LiamNeural) 🌌 Produced by Dr. Elara Explores #DarkEnergy #Cosmology #UniverseExpansion #SpaceFacts #Astrophysics #ScienceShorts #BigBang #Physics #Astronomy",Dr. Elara Explores,1.2K
Restoring an Agilent E3610A Bench Power Supply: Capacitor Replacement & Fan Upgrade,"The Agilent (now Keysight) E3610A is a workhorse bench power supply, but after decades of service, these units often suffer from dried-out electrolytic capacitors leading to ripple issues and reduced stability. Furthermore, the original fan can be quite noisy. In this video, we'll go through a full recapitation process, replacing key electrolytic capacitors on both the main board and the output stage to restore stable, clean power. We'll also upgrade the noisy stock fan with a modern, quieter equivalent, significantly improving the lab environment. This DIY repair not only extends the life of a valuable piece of test equipment but also makes it more pleasant to use. Parts Used: - Main Filter Capacitors: 2x 4700uF 50V Low ESR - Output Stage Capacitors: 4x 1000uF 35V Low ESR - Quiet Fan: Noctua NF-A4x10 FLX (40x10mm, 12V). You can find these parts at major electronics distributors like Mouser or Digi-Key. --- Check out my other repair and restoration videos here: [Link to channel videos] --- #BenchPowerSupply #AgilentE3610A #ElectronicsRepair #CapacitorReplacement #TestEquipment",LabGear Restore,1750
