"Symposium on Digital Aesthetics: 2024 Design & Society Series: Opening Address: Bruce Sterling, “The Algorithmic Sublime”","On Friday, October 25, 2024, the Global Institute for Design Ethics presented its annual “Symposium on Digital Aesthetics,” exploring the evolving relationship between technology, beauty, and human values. Organized by doctoral candidates and faculty from the Department of Computational Design, and introduced by lead researcher Dr. Anya Sharma, the symposium brought together leading thinkers to critically examine the aesthetic dimensions of the digital age. The opening address was delivered by acclaimed author and futurist Bruce Sterling, whose talk, “The Algorithmic Sublime,” delved into the profound, often unsettling, beauty and complexity emerging from autonomous systems and AI-generated art. Other sessions throughout the day addressed: the ethical implications of data-driven aesthetics; the role of designers in shaping future digital experiences; the visual language of synthetic media; and how virtual environments redefine perceptions of space and form.",Global Institute for Design Ethics,5
