#67 Deep Learning for Spatial Transcriptomics: Unveiling Cellular Neighborhoods with Dr. Anya Sharma,"Dr. Anya Sharma (https://anyasharma.lab.com) presents a cutting-edge deep learning methodology designed to revolutionize the analysis of spatial transcriptomics data. Traditional methods often struggle with the inherent sparsity and noise in spatial data, making it challenging to accurately identify intricate cellular neighborhoods and their functional interactions. Dr. Sharma's novel framework, built upon graph neural networks and variational autoencoders, offers a robust solution for denoising, dimensionality reduction, and the precise delineation of spatially co-localized cell populations. This approach significantly enhances the resolution of tissue microenvironments, enabling researchers to uncover previously hidden biological insights from complex spatial omics datasets, and paving the way for more accurate disease modeling and therapeutic discovery. We also briefly touch upon her work on integrating multi-modal spatial data. Links: • Her recent publication: ""GraphVAE: A variational autoencoder for spatial transcriptomics"" (Journal of Computational Biology, 2024) • GitHub Repository: https://github.com/asharma/GraphVAE_spatial • Lab Website: https://anyasharma.lab.com/research",The Computational Biology Forum,3
