BOOK DESCRIPTION

Imagine a world where early Christian thought diverged into countless paths, some leading to profound mystical insight, others deemed heresy. In Decoding the Nag Hammadi Scriptures, Dr. Evelyn Reed meticulously unearths the hidden narratives of the Gnostic texts discovered in Egypt. These ancient manuscripts reveal a different understanding of creation, humanity's divine spark, and the nature of salvation, challenging conventional interpretations of early Christianity.

Join Dr. Reed as she guides listeners through these complex and enigmatic writings, illuminating their historical context, philosophical depth, and spiritual relevance for today. Discover the voices of figures like Mary Magdalene, Thomas, and Valentinus, and uncover the Gnostic path to self-knowledge and liberation.

Highlights:
• The diverse origins and meanings of Gnostic cosmology
• Insights into the roles of Sophia and the Demiurge
• Meditative practices found within Gnostic teachings
• The radical concept of innate divinity and self-salvation

—
ABOUT THE AUTHOR

Dr. Evelyn Reed is a distinguished scholar in Comparative Religious Studies and ancient languages, with a particular focus on Coptic and Hellenistic Greek. She holds professorships at the Institute for Esoteric Studies and is a leading voice in bringing ancient mystical texts to a wider audience. Her previous works include ""The Gospel of Mary: A New Perspective"" and ""Mysteries of the Desert Fathers."" Dr. Reed frequently lectures internationally on Gnosticism, Hermeticism, and the spiritual traditions of the Near East.

