The Shocking Experiment That Showed We All Obey Orders #psychology #history #shorts,"In the early 1960s, Yale psychologist Stanley Milgram conducted a series of controversial experiments to understand human obedience to authority. Participants were instructed to administer what they believed were increasingly painful electric shocks to another person (an actor). The results were chilling: a significant number of participants continued to obey the experimenter's commands, even when they heard the 'learner' cry out in pain. This is the disturbing story of how far ordinary people will go when told to follow orders, revealing a fundamental, and often frightening, aspect of human nature. ⚡️ A lesson in the power of authority and conformity.",The Hidden Depths,450
