IB MATH AA/AI HL CALCULUS: CHAIN RULE & IMPLICIT DIFFERENTIATION,"‍ Mastering Differentiation: Chain Rule & Implicit Differentiation | IB Mathematics AA HL / SL

Welcome to IB Math Mastery  — your ultimate guide to excelling in IB Mathematics with clear explanations and comprehensive problem-solving!

In this lesson, we dive deep into two crucial calculus techniques: the Chain Rule and Implicit Differentiation. These concepts are fundamental for both Paper 1 and Paper 2 in IB Mathematics (AA HL / SL), and mastering them is key to achieving a top score.

This video breaks down each concept step-by-step with practical IB-style examples to help you build confidence and accuracy in your calculations.

 What You Will Learn in This Lesson

 Understanding the Chain Rule for composite functions
 Applying the Chain Rule in various contexts
 Grasping the concept of implicit differentiation
 Differentiating equations where y is not explicitly defined
 Solving complex IB-style questions involving both techniques

 Key Concepts

✔ Chain Rule → Differentiating a function of a function (e.g., f(g(x)))
✔ Implicit Differentiation → Differentiating terms with respect to x when y is an implicit function of x
✔ Derivatives → Rate of change, gradient of a tangent, crucial for understanding function behavior

 Why This Topic Is Important

Understanding Chain Rule and Implicit Differentiation helps you:

✔ Solve a wider range of differentiation problems
✔ Tackle advanced calculus questions in Paper 1 and Paper 2
✔ Develop strong analytical skills for related rates and optimization
