Earthquake in Lombok Today | Strong Tremors Shake Indonesia | Breaking News,"#LombokEarthquake #EarthquakeIndonesia #Indonesia #BreakingNews #EarthquakeAlert #IndonesiaNews #NaturalDisaster #Tremors #Lombok #earthquaketoday A powerful earthquake has struck Lombok, Indonesia, causing widespread panic and sending tremors across the region. Initial reports indicate residents rushed from their homes and buildings as the ground shook violently. Emergency services are on high alert, and authorities are assessing the situation. While the full extent of the damage is yet to be determined, there are early concerns about structural integrity and potential casualties. Lombok, part of Indonesia's 'Ring of Fire,' is frequently affected by seismic activity, making earthquake preparedness a critical aspect of daily life. Today's event serves as a stark reminder of the region's vulnerability. Eyewitnesses describe a terrifying ordeal, with many sharing their experiences and videos on social media platforms. The incident highlights the urgent need for robust disaster response and community resilience.",SouthAsia Today,4850
Automating Vulnerability Discovery in IoT Firmware: Introducing FirmHunter,"From Embedded Security Summit 2024, watch Dr. Anya Sharma's talk: Automating Vulnerability Discovery in IoT Firmware: Introducing FirmHunter.

Talk Slides: https://github.com/securefirm/presentations/blob/main/ESS24/FirmHunter.pdf

The proliferation of Internet of Things (IoT) devices has created an expansive and often vulnerable attack surface. Manually auditing the firmware of these diverse devices for security flaws is a labor-intensive, time-consuming, and often incomplete process. This talk addresses the critical need for scalable and efficient methods to identify vulnerabilities within proprietary and third-party IoT firmware.

We introduce FirmHunter, a new open-source automated framework designed to streamline the process of finding security flaws in IoT firmware. Built on a foundation of emulation (leveraging QEMU), advanced static analysis, and guided dynamic analysis, FirmHunter provides a robust pipeline for uncovering hidden backdoors, hardcoded credentials, buffer overflows, and other critical vulnerabilities across various architectures (ARM, MIPS, RISC-V).

Unlike traditional approaches that often rely on manual reverse engineering or limited pattern matching, FirmHunter integrates symbolic execution and taint analysis on emulated firmware execution paths. This allows for deep introspection into program behavior, even in the absence of source code or debugging symbols. We will detail its architecture, capabilities, and the methodologies employed to handle the complexities of different embedded environments and proprietary binaries.

Our contribution includes comprehensive benchmarks and real-world case studies demonstrating FirmHunter's efficacy in identifying previously unknown vulnerabilities in widely deployed IoT devices. We will also release FirmHunter to the security community, fostering collaborative development and improvement in the continuous effort to secure the IoT landscape.",Embedded Security Summit,480
