Ashwagandha — The Ancient Adaptogen That Calms Stress and Boosts Focus,"A comprehensive review published in 'Phytomedicine Reports' (2024) synthesized findings from 15 double-blind, placebo-controlled trials on Ashwagandha (Withania somnifera) for stress and anxiety. The results consistently demonstrated a significant reduction in perceived stress levels and cortisol markers.

Ashwagandha is an adaptogen, meaning it helps your body adapt to stress. Its active compounds, withanolides, modulate the HPA axis (hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis), reducing cortisol production and promoting a sense of calm. Unlike many anxiolytics, Ashwagandha doesn't cause drowsiness or dependency, instead enhancing mental clarity and focus.

The effective dose in most studies ranged from 300-600 mg of standardized root extract daily. Revered in Ayurvedic medicine for over 3,000 years, this powerful herb is now gaining recognition for its modern applications.

Know someone struggling with daily stress? Share this video with them.
#Ashwagandha #Adaptogens #NaturalStressRelief #MentalClarity #VitalRoots #HerbalMedicine",Vital Roots,135
