Decoding Your DNA: Pharmacogenomics & The Future of Personalized Prescribing | Precision Pharma Update,"Episode Overview: This episode of Precision Pharma Update delves into the transformative field of pharmacogenomics (PGx) and its growing role in shaping personalized medicine. We explore how understanding an individual's genetic makeup can optimize drug selection, dosage, and minimize adverse reactions, revolutionizing patient care within the pharmacy setting. Join us as we discuss the science, implementation challenges, and future potential of PGx with leading experts.

Segment 1 – The Science of PGx: From Genes to Optimal Dosing with Dr. Elena Petrova
We welcome Dr. Elena Petrova, a leading pharmacogeneticist from GenomRx Institute, to demystify the principles of pharmacogenomics. Dr. Petrova explains how genetic variations influence drug metabolism and response, providing pharmacists with critical insights to tailor medication therapies. This segment covers the core concepts, common PGx markers, and the clinical implications for various drug classes.

Segment 2 – Implementing PGx in Practice: Clinical Integration & Workflow with PharmaGen Solutions
Next, we're joined by Michael Chen, CEO of PharmaGen Solutions, to discuss the practical integration of pharmacogenomic testing into daily pharmacy workflows. Michael shares strategies for incorporating PGx results into patient counseling, electronic health records, and clinical decision support systems. He highlights how pharmacies are leveraging technology to deliver actionable genetic insights, improving medication safety and efficacy in real-world settings.

Segment 3 – The Future Landscape of Personalized Pharmacy: Challenges & Opportunities with Dr. Sarah Jenkins
In our final segment, Dr. Sarah Jenkins, Director of Clinical Pharmacy Innovation at Vanguard Health Systems, explores the opportunities and hurdles facing personalized pharmacy. Dr. Jenkins discusses the ethical considerations, regulatory frameworks, reimbursement models, and educational needs required to scale PGx adoption. She offers a forward-looking perspective on how pharmacists will be central to delivering precision medicine in the coming decade.

Special thanks to this week’s sponsors: GenomRx Institute for advancing genetic research and PharmaGen Solutions for innovative clinical decision support tools.

About Precision Pharma Update: Precision Pharma Update delivers in-depth discussions and expert interviews on cutting-edge advancements, research, and technologies shaping the future of pharmacy and personalized healthcare.",Precision Pharma Insights,65
