Feature Engineering for Machine Learning Part I - Foundations by Dr. Anya Sharma,"Feature Engineering for Machine Learning Part I - Foundations by Dr. Anya Sharma | Apex Data Science Academy | #FeatureEngineering #MachineLearning #DataScience #AI #DeepLearning #DataPreprocessing #MLOps #ComputerScience #UniversityLectures  Description  This video, 'Feature Engineering for Machine Learning Part I - Foundations,' delves into the critical initial stages of transforming raw data into features that can be effectively used by machine learning algorithms. Feature Engineering is a foundational step in the machine learning pipeline, significantly impacting model performance and interpretability. This first part covers the core concepts and fundamental techniques necessary to prepare your data for robust model training.  We will explore: *   Understanding different data types (numerical, categorical, temporal) and their implications for feature engineering. *   Basic data transformation methods: scaling, normalization, and binning. *   Strategies for handling missing values and outliers in a feature engineering context. *   Introduction to creating new features from existing ones to capture more information.  Mastering these foundational concepts of Feature Engineering (Part I) is crucial for anyone looking to build effective and high-performing machine learning models, laying the groundwork for more advanced techniques discussed in subsequent parts.  #FeatureEngineering #MachineLearning #DataScience #AI #DeepLearning #DataPreprocessing #MLOps #ComputerScience #UniversityLectures #TechEducation #DataAnalytics #DataTransformation #ModelTraining",Apex Data Science Academy,12
