Unpacking the 'Invisible Hand': A System Dynamics Perspective on Market Failures,"#systemdynamics #marketfailures #economicmodeling #systemsthinking The presentation delves into the complexities of Adam Smith's 'invisible hand' theory, exploring instances where unregulated markets lead to inefficient or undesirable outcomes. Using system dynamics, we will model common market failures such as externalities (pollution), public goods provision, and information asymmetry, demonstrating how feedback loops and time delays can amplify these issues. This session includes practical examples modeled in Vensim, illustrating how policy interventions can be designed to steer markets towards more socially optimal equilibria. We will discuss the limitations of static equilibrium analysis and highlight the dynamic nature of market adjustments, challenging conventional assumptions about market efficiency. The Q&A segment will cover topics like behavioral economics' role in dynamic models, the effectiveness of various regulatory mechanisms, and the application of these models to contemporary economic challenges like climate change and healthcare access. Discover how a systems approach offers deeper insights into economic phenomena beyond traditional equilibrium-based analyses.",Dynamic Economy Insights,155
