"కనిపెట్టేశా రెస్టారెంట్ స్టైల్ క్రిస్పీ దోస # ఈ 3టిప్స్ తో # బంగారు రంగులో,పలుచగా పేపర్ లాగా#దోస","hotal style dosa#crispy dosa#dosa recipe

crispy dosa recipe|how to make crispy dosa|golden dosa recipe|dosa batter recipe|thin crispy dosa|south indian dosa|restaurant style dosa|perfect dosa batter|easy breakfast recipe|cooking|Golden Spatula Kitchen

Learn the secret trick to make crispy, golden and paper-thin dosas at home.
Using simple ingredients like rice, urad dal and fenugreek, you can make perfect dosa batter.

Follow this easy South Indian breakfast recipe and enjoy restaurant-style crispy dosas every time.

✔ Crispy Dosa
✔ Golden Texture
✔ Perfect Fermentation Trick

Try this simple method and your dosas will come out crispy, golden and delicious every time

Hello friends today we are going to prepare dosa.

1️⃣ Take 3 cups rice and 1 cup urad dal. Add 1 tsp fenugreek seeds. Wash them well and soak for 5-6 hours.
2️⃣ After soaking, drain the water and grind the rice and urad dal mixture into a smooth, slightly coarse batter. Add water as needed.
3️⃣ Transfer the batter to a large bowl, add salt and mix well. Leave the batter to ferment overnight (8-12 hours) in a warm place.
4️⃣ After fermentation, gently mix the batter. Adjust consistency with a little water if needed – it should be pourable but not too watery.
5️⃣ Heat a non-stick or cast iron dosa pan. Season it with a sliced onion dipped in oil for the first dosa. Reduce heat to medium.
6️⃣ Pour a ladleful of batter onto the hot pan, spread it evenly in a circular motion from the center outwards to form a thin dosa.
7️⃣ Drizzle a little oil or ghee around the edges and cook until golden brown and crispy. Fold and serve hot.

