Algorithmic Justice: When AI Replaces the Judge | Ethical AI in Law,"Artificial Intelligence is rapidly entering every domain of human life, and the justice system is no exception. From predictive policing and risk assessments to automating legal research and even assisting in sentencing decisions, AI promises efficiency but introduces profound ethical dilemmas.

In this video, we delve into the burgeoning field of algorithmic justice, examining how AI is being deployed in courts and law enforcement. We explore the potential benefits – faster processing, data-driven insights – alongside the critical risks: algorithmic bias, lack of transparency, and the erosion of fundamental human rights.

Can an algorithm truly deliver justice? What happens when AI makes a mistake in a legal context? We discuss the urgent need for robust regulatory frameworks, accountability mechanisms, and ethical guidelines to ensure that technology serves justice, not undermines it.

Join us as we explore the future of law in the age of AI, asking whether we are prepared for a world where code, not conscience, dictates fate.

