The Alignment Problem in AGI: A Technical Deep Dive into Value Alignment,"Presented at the annual 'Frontiers in AI Research' conference on October 27, 2024, this lecture provides an in-depth exploration of the Artificial General Intelligence (AGI) alignment problem. We delve into the philosophical underpinnings and technical challenges of ensuring future advanced AI systems operate in accordance with human values and intentions. The talk covers various approaches to alignment, including reward modeling, interpretability, and agent corrigibility. Accompanying slides and additional resources can be found on our research institute's website: https://www.thealgorithmicacademy.org/lectures/alignment-agi Subscribe to our mailing list for updates on new research and events: https://www.thealgorithmicacademy.org/newsletter Timestamps: 00:00 Introduction to AGI and the Alignment Challenge 07:30 Formalizing Human Values: Difficulties and Approaches 19:15 Outer vs. Inner Alignment: Understanding the Discrepancy 32:00 Reward Hacking, Specification Gaming, and Wireheading 45:40 Interpretability and Explainable AI (XAI) as Alignment Tools 58:05 Robustness and Adversarial Examples in Aligned Systems 01:09:20 Current Research Initiatives and Open Problems 01:20:00 Q&A Session",The Algorithmic Academy,350
