Fenbendazole & Cancer: 4 Surprising Anti-Tumor Pathways Mainstream Medicine Ignores,"Is Fenbendazole the unexpected cancer fighter gaining traction in alternative health circles? A molecular biologist with 15 years in oncology research dives into the 4 scientifically observed mechanisms by which this common anti-parasitic drug may exert anti-cancer effects at the cellular level. This discussion highlights the burgeoning field of drug repurposing, emphasizing the preliminary nature of current data and the critical need for robust clinical trials to establish efficacy and safety. Understanding the underlying cellular pharmacology is essential for informed discussions. This is NOT medical advice or a cure claim.   In this video:  How Fenbendazole disrupts microtubule formation, halting cancer cell division. How it inhibits glucose uptake, effectively starving cancer cells. Its role in enhancing apoptosis (programmed cell death) in various cancer cell lines. Its potential to modulate the immune system for anti-tumor responses. Why there's limited funding for large-scale human trials (and what that means for you). The importance of understanding bioavailability and proper dosing strategies.  This video is for educational purposes only. Always consult your oncologist or healthcare provider before making any medical decisions.   CHAPTERS  00:00 — Introduction: Fenbendazole & Cancer Research  02:15 — Mechanism 1: Microtubule Disruption & Cell Cycle Arrest  04:05 — Mechanism 2: Glucose Metabolism Inhibition (Starving Cancer)  06:30 — Mechanism 3: Enhancing Apoptosis (Programmed Cell Death)  08:45 — Mechanism 4: Immune System Modulation  10:10 — The Clinical Gap: Why isn't it widely studied?  12:00 — Understanding Bioavailability & Dosing Considerations  14:30 — Conclusion & Future Outlook   Medical Disclaimer This video is for educational purposes only and is not medical advice. Do not start, stop, or change any supplement or medication without speaking with your physician/pharmacist—especially if you have a pre-existing medical condition or are on other medications.  The information presented in the following video are based upon the experience and training of the presenter and scientific information currently available. The suggestions in this presentation are not meant to be a substitute for medical evaluation and treatment. The presenter does not recommend changing or adding medications or supplements without consulting your personal physician. The presenter specifically disclaims any liability arising directly or indirectly from the use of this presentation.  CONTACT INFO:  Cellular Health Unlocked  Ph # 555-123-4567  Hours: 9am-5pm EST M-F Email: info@cellularhealthunlocked.com",Cellular Health Unlocked,52345
