Why Can't We Go Back? The Unsolved Mystery of Time's Arrow,"We move forward through time, never backward. But why? The laws of physics seem to work perfectly well in reverse, yet our universe stubbornly marches in one direction. This profound enigma, known as the arrow of time, challenges our deepest understanding of reality. In this video, we explore the thermodynamic arrow (entropy and the Second Law), the cosmological arrow (the expansion of the universe), and the psychological arrow (our memory). From Boltzmann's statistical mechanics to the very origins of the Big Bang, we trace the scientific pursuit to explain why time has a direction, and what it would mean if it didn't. Join us as we unravel one of the most persistent and philosophical questions in all of physics. Topics: arrow of time, entropy, thermodynamics, Boltzmann, Big Bang, cosmology, quantum gravity, fundamental physics, philosophy of time. Leave your thoughts in the comments — what's your take on time's flow? Subscribe for more deep dives into the cosmos.

