How Skyscrapers Defy Earthquakes & High Winds | Engineering Wonders Explained | #shorts,"How do the world's tallest buildings stand strong against nature's fury? 🏗️Building skyscrapers in earthquake-prone regions or areas with high winds requires cutting-edge engineering to ensure their safety and stability.To prevent catastrophic failure, engineers employ a combination of innovative techniques to absorb and dissipate energy.One key method is the use of 'tuned mass dampers' – massive pendulums installed near the top of the building that swing to counteract the building's sway. Another crucial technique is 'base isolation,' where the entire structure rests on flexible bearings that absorb ground motion during an earthquake.Additionally, skyscrapers are designed with deep foundations, reinforced concrete cores, and flexible steel frames that allow them to flex rather than break under extreme stress.These ingenious engineering solutions ensure that these towering marvels remain stable, safe, and iconic for decades to come.#Skyscraper #BuildingDesign #EarthquakeProof#WindResistance #StructuralEngineering#ModernArchitecture #CivilEngineering#MegaProjects #UrbanPlanning#EngineeringFacts #ConstructionFacts#TechnologyFacts #BuildingSafety #Damper#BaseIsolation #AmazingFacts #InterestingFacts #DidYouKnow #FactShorts #UnknownFacts #Shorts#YouTubeShorts #TrendingShorts #ViralShorts#Explore #ViralVideo",Engineering Deep Dive,2450000
