How lichens act as natural air quality indicators
Their crucial role in soil formation and nutrient cycling
The slow but powerful impact of lichens on ecosystems
Hidden microscopic structures that enable their survival
How lichens provide food and shelter for small creatures
The potential for lichens in medicine and biomonitoring

