Earth's Green Pulse: 1-Year Global Vegetation Timelapse | MODIS NDVI (2023),"Witness the breathtaking annual cycle of Earth's vegetation as it breathes, expands, and recedes across the globe. This 1-year timelapse uses Normalized Difference Vegetation Index (NDVI) data from NASA's MODIS satellite, showcasing the dynamic health and density of plant life throughout 2023.

🌿 UNDERSTANDING NDVI
NDVI quantifies vegetation by measuring the difference between near-infrared (which vigorous vegetation strongly reflects) and red light (which vegetation absorbs).
  • High NDVI values (vibrant green) indicate dense, healthy vegetation.
  • Low NDVI values (brown, tan) represent sparse vegetation, barren land, or water.

🌍 VISUALIZED SEASONALITY
Observe the dramatic shifts:
  • The green wave sweeping across the Northern Hemisphere with spring and summer.
  • The distinct wet and dry seasons in tropical regions.
  • The subtle yet critical changes in desert fringes and polar regions.
  • Key insights into agricultural cycles, forest health, and desertification trends.

🛰️ DATA & PROCESSING
• Satellite: NASA Terra & Aqua (MODIS instrument)
• Data Product: MODIS/Terra + Aqua Vegetation Index (MOD13A2/MYD13A2), 16-day composites, 1km resolution.
• Timeframe: January 1, 2023 – December 31, 2023
• Source: NASA LP DAAC
• Pipeline: Google Earth Engine (GEE) for data extraction and processing, Python for visualization and animation.

