Full of tiny builders, showing off their grace!
Little polyps growing, side by side, so bright
Sharing food with algae, shining in the light!
From the smallest fish to the biggest whale's quest
The coral reef ecosystem puts life to the test!

(Verse 2)
What makes the coral shine, green, red, and blue?
Tiny little algae, helping them get through!
They live inside the polyps, a partnership so grand
Giving food and color, all across the land (under the sea, understand!)
But if the water gets too warm or something's not right
The algae pack their bags and swim out of sight!
Then the coral gets stressed, turns white and then pale
Oh, that's called bleaching, a very sad tale!

(Bridge)
(Rhythm slows, somber synth pads, then builds)
We need to protect them, with all of our might
Keep our oceans healthy, shining ever so bright!
Small actions make a difference, you and me
For the future of the reef, and all the life we see!
(Beat drops back in!)

(Chorus)
Oh! The coral reef is a magical place
Full of tiny builders, showing off their grace!
Little polyps growing, side by side, so bright
Sharing food with algae, shining in the light!
From the smallest fish to the biggest whale's quest
The coral reef ecosystem puts life to the test!

(Outro)
Keep learning!
Keep caring!
Coral and Finnegan, swimming out!
(Fades with tropical percussion and water sounds)

