Automated Program Synthesis with Datalog and SMT Solvers,"This talk explores cutting-edge techniques in automated program synthesis, focusing on the synergy between declarative logic programming (specifically Datalog) and Satisfiability Modulo Theories (SMT) solvers. We discuss how Datalog can be leveraged to generate candidate program structures and specifications, while SMT solvers provide a robust mechanism for verifying correctness and finding counterexamples efficiently. The presentation will cover challenges in search space exploration, handling complex data structures, and recent advancements that enable synthesizing non-trivial programs from sparse specifications. A practical demonstration using an open-source framework (e.g., SynthLib++) will illustrate its application in domains like data transformation and protocol synthesis. Speaker: Dr. Elena Petrova, Lead Researcher at Algorithmic Systems Lab. Date: 2024-11-15",Formal Methods Insights,58
