Cloud Storage Leaks: How a Simple Setting Exposes Your Data to Hackers,"Misconfigured cloud storage is a pervasive and often overlooked vulnerability that can lead to massive data breaches. From publicly exposed Amazon S3 buckets to insecure Azure Blob Storage, organizations frequently make critical errors in setting up their cloud assets, inadvertently granting unauthorized access to sensitive information. In this video, we'll dive into how these misconfigurations occur, the types of data at risk, and the methods attackers use to discover and exploit these open doors. We'll explore real-world examples and provide actionable steps for preventing cloud storage leaks, including proper access control, encryption, and continuous monitoring. Understanding cloud security fundamentals is essential for anyone working with modern infrastructure. Protect your data, protect your reputation. Subscribe for more insights into cloud security, devsecops, and ethical hacking.",SecureStack,820
