The Artist Exposing AI's Hidden Biases with Data Art,"Artificial Intelligence is often presented as an objective force, but for computational artist Maya Singh, it's a canvas for exposing human flaws. Her captivating art installations don't just fill galleries; they lay bare the intricate biases woven into the algorithms that shape our world.

Inspired by the material reality of AI, Maya's work highlights that data isn't neutral. We trace her journey from traditional art schools to becoming a pioneer in data visualization, transforming abstract concepts of algorithmic injustice into striking visual experiences. From her 'Ghost in the Machine' series, which vividly maps bias in predictive policing, to 'The Algorithmic Gaze,' a critical commentary on facial recognition's racial and gender blind spots, Maya's art forces us to confront uncomfortable truths.

Her methods combine programming, data science, and artistic expression to reveal how historical inequalities are encoded and amplified by AI systems. Maya argues that without constant human scrutiny and creative intervention, AI risks becoming a powerful, yet prejudiced, mirror of society. This deep dive will change how you perceive the 'intelligence' behind your screens and the ethical dimensions of our digital future.

#dataart #aiforbias #artandtech #ethicalai #digitalactivism #computationalart",Digital Uncovered,1250
