"Contaminated Water in Pani Puri? Student Alleges Unhygienic Practices at Popular FC Road Stall, Pune","A university student in Pune has raised serious concerns about the hygiene standards at a popular Pani Puri stall on FC Road. The student claims he observed the vendor using tap water directly from an unverified source to prepare the Pani Puri, rather than filtered or bottled water, raising fears of contamination.

The incident, which was partially filmed and shared on social media, quickly went viral among local groups, sparking a wider discussion about food safety and the health risks associated with street food. FC Road is a bustling hub for students and food enthusiasts, making this revelation particularly alarming.

Following the online uproar, local health activists and resident welfare associations have called upon the Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) and the Food and Drug Administration (FDA) to conduct immediate inspections of street food vendors, especially those in high-footfall areas. So far, neither the stall owner nor the authorities have issued a public statement regarding the allegations.

Have you ever questioned the hygiene at your favourite street food stall? Share your experiences and tips for spotting unhygienic practices in the comments below.

#PuneFood #StreetFoodSafety #FCRoad #ConsumerAlert #PuneNews #FoodHygiene",Pune Insight,3150
