Funding isn't just about a great idea; it's about a compelling strategy.
Why ""traction"" in MedTech is different from consumer tech, and how to demonstrate it.
The crucial data points investors demand before writing a check.
How to value your MedTech company realistically without underselling your potential.
Avoiding common dilution mistakes that cripple future funding rounds.
Building an investor deck that speaks their language, not just yours.
Strategic partnerships: When they're a blessing, and when they're a trap.

If you're a MedTech founder struggling to attract the right investors, or preparing for your next funding round, this episode is packed with actionable insights you won't want to miss.

