Classic International Harvester Plows Through Fields! #VintageTractor #FarmallPower #OldIron,"Witness the timeless power of this classic International Harvester Farmall M tractor as it effortlessly turns soil! Watch a piece of farming history bring fields to life with its iconic rumble and steadfast performance. A true testament to old-school agricultural engineering and reliability.

Tool Name:
International Harvester Farmall M Tractor with 3-Bottom Plow (Vintage)

Estimated Price:
$8,000 – $20,000 (restored, depending on condition and implements)

Specifications:
Engine: Gasoline/Kerosene (approx. 40-50 HP)
Plow Type: Mounted or semi-mounted 3-bottom moldboard plow
Operating Speed: 3-5 mph (plowing)
Transmission: Manual (5 forward, 1 reverse)
Drive Type: 2WD
Build Era: 1939–1952 (Farmall M)

Advantages:
✔ Iconic design and historical significance
✔ Relatively simple to maintain and repair
✔ Durable and robust construction
✔ Excellent for small to medium-scale plowing tasks
✔ Strong community and parts availability

Disadvantages:
✖ Lower fuel efficiency than modern tractors
✖ Open station (no cab, less comfort)
✖ Slower operating speed for large fields
✖ Limited hydraulics compared to newer models

Working Principle:
The tractor pulls the moldboard plow, which consists of multiple bottoms. Each moldboard cuts a furrow slice, lifts it, and inverts it, burying weeds and crop residue while aerating the soil, preparing it for planting.

Productivity Impact:
For its era, the Farmall M significantly mechanized farm labor, allowing a single farmer to plow much larger areas than with horses. Today, it remains a capable machine for preparing smaller fields, garden plots, or for historical farming demonstrations, preserving traditional agricultural practices.

