The Yellowstone Eruption: A Timeline of Global Catastrophe?,"The eruption of a supervolcano is not just a geological event; it's a profound challenge to life on Earth. 

In this 'Chronicles of Catastrophe' deep dive, we explore a hypothetical scenario: a major eruption of the Yellowstone Caldera. We break down the cascading effects across time, drawing on scientific models and geological history:

Milliseconds to hours: immediate blast, ashfall, pyroclastic flows, local devastation
Hours to days: regional ash plumes, atmospheric disruption, air travel halt, infrastructure damage
Weeks to months: global climate shifts ('volcanic winter'), agricultural failures, societal breakdown
Months to years: long-term ecological impacts, humanitarian crises, geopolitical instability

This episode aims to educate on the immense power of geological forces and their potential global impact. Always rely on official scientific bodies for real-world guidance.

