Zircon-Rutile Geochronology Reveals Pulsed Magmatic-Hydrothermal Fluid Flow in Critical Raw Material Deposits,"Understanding the timing and mechanisms of critical raw material (CRM) enrichment in magmatic-hydrothermal systems is paramount for effective exploration. This seminar presents new U-Pb and Lu-Hf isotopic data from zircon and rutile separates collected from the Kamoa-Kakula copper-cobalt deposit in the Central African Copperbelt. Our findings demonstrate distinct, episodic fluid pulses associated with successive stages of mineralization and reveal insights into the evolving source reservoirs of ore-forming fluids. These results provide a novel framework for deciphering complex magmatic-hydrothermal ore genesis and improving predictive models for deep-seated CRM occurrences.",Global Geometallurgy Network,12
