Decarbonizing Buildings: Strategies for EPBD Compliance and Future Readiness - EcoBuild Summit 2027,"At the EcoBuild Summit 2027, we spoke with Dr. Elena Rossi, Head of Policy and Innovation at GreenTech Solutions, to explore the impact of the latest EU Energy Performance of Buildings Directive (EPBD) recast on the European construction sector. The conversation delves into the urgent need for deep retrofits and the integration of advanced sustainable technologies.Dr. Rossi highlights that while the EPBD sets ambitious targets, the lack of consistent financial mechanisms and skilled labor presents significant hurdles for widespread adoption. We discuss the critical role of long-term policy stability and accessible funding to enable homeowners and developers to invest confidently in energy-efficient solutions.The discussion also shifts to a paradigm beyond mere compliance, emphasizing the economic benefits and enhanced liveability of high-performance buildings. GreenTech Solutions' ""Circular Building Model,"" showcased at the summit, integrates advanced insulation, smart energy management systems, and on-site renewable generation to create truly net-zero structures.The residential sector, moving past initial renewable energy installations, is now seeing increased demand for holistic, integrated systems that combine heating, cooling, ventilation, and power storage. Dr. Rossi underscores the rising importance of sustainable materials and the circular economy in building design and construction.Technologically, GreenTech Solutions is advocating for scalable district heating and cooling networks powered by renewable sources, alongside a strong push for intelligent building management systems that optimize energy consumption in real-time. This approach not only aids in decarbonization but also enhances the resilience and energy independence of communities.",Sustainable Systems Pro,75
