AI Chatbot for Technical Manuals | RAG + Fine-tuning Explained | My ML Internship Project,"This video details my Machine Learning Internship project, where I developed an AI-powered chatbot designed to answer questions from complex technical manuals using a combination of Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) and Large Language Model (LLM) fine-tuning.

The project aimed to create an intelligent system that can quickly retrieve relevant information from vast technical documentation and generate precise, context-aware answers to user queries, significantly improving efficiency for engineers and support staff.

✅ Project Overview:
• Implemented a robust RAG pipeline for information retrieval
• Fine-tuned an open-source LLM for domain-specific understanding
• Integrated a vector database (e.g., ChromaDB, Milvus) for semantic search
• Designed an interactive chatbot interface for user interaction

⚙️ Approach:
• Curated and preprocessed technical documentation datasets
• Generated embeddings for document chunks and stored them efficiently
• Fine-tuned a Transformer-based LLM on a Q&A dataset derived from the manuals
• Developed a query processing pipeline combining retrieval results with LLM generation

⚠️ Challenges Faced:
• Handling highly technical jargon and complex diagrams within documents
• Ensuring factual accuracy and minimizing hallucinations from the LLM
• Optimizing retrieval speed and relevance for large datasets

📗 Key Learnings:
• Deep dive into practical RAG architecture implementation
• Hands-on experience with LLM fine-tuning techniques
• Understanding the synergy between retrieval and generation in AI systems
• Real-world problem-solving in natural language processing

🛠️ Skills Developed:
• Applied Machine Learning & NLP
• Large Language Model (LLM) Engineering
• Vector Database Management
• Python Programming & System Design

This project provided invaluable insights into building practical AI solutions for enterprise knowledge management.

