JWST Stunned By Unexplained Volcanic Activity on Distant Exoplanet,"The James Webb Space Telescope (JWST) continues to redefine our understanding of the cosmos, and its latest observations of the exoplanet LHS 475 b have left scientists astonished. Orbiting a red dwarf star just 41 light-years away, this Earth-sized world was initially thought to be a relatively calm, rocky body. However, detailed spectroscopic analysis by JWST has revealed anomalous and persistent infrared emissions emanating from its surface, strongly indicative of widespread and sustained volcanic activity. This unexpected geological dynamism challenges current models of small, rocky planet evolution, especially for a world tidally locked and orbiting so close to its star. What's driving these intense planetary eruptions? Scientists are grappling with theories, from internal tidal heating more extreme than anticipated to an unusually large and active core for a planet of its size. The discovery suggests that volcanic activity might be far more common on exoplanets than previously believed, potentially influencing their atmospheric compositions and, by extension, their capacity for harboring life. This groundbreaking data from JWST is pushing the boundaries of exoplanetary science, offering new clues into the fiery hearts of distant worlds and the intricate processes that shape them across the galaxy. — ABOUT THIS CHANNEL Cosmic Chronicles unravels the mysteries of the universe through stunning documentaries, bringing you the latest breakthroughs in astrophysics, planetary science, and the search for extraterrestrial life. Subscribe and explore the cosmos with us, one discovery at a time. — ✨ Instagram: @cosmicchroniclesofficial ▶️ YouTube: @cosmicchronicles •• TikTok: @cosmicchronicles — CREDITS Video Credit: NASA / ESA / CSA / STScI Music: Licensed via Epidemic Sound — DISCLAIMER This video is created for educational and informational purposes, presenting scientific discoveries and space exploration missions. — HASHTAGS #JWST #exoplanet #volcano #space #nasa #esa #astronomy #cosmos #spaceexploration #science #cosmicchronicles",Cosmic Chronicles,1500
