Stop Leaks Dead: Flange Gaskets Explained #shorts,"A gasket is a critical mechanical seal used to prevent leakage between two mating surfaces, most commonly in piping and pressure systems. These seemingly simple components are vital for maintaining system integrity and operational safety.

🔶 Working Principle

• Placed between two flanges or surfaces.
• Compressed by bolts, conforming to surface irregularities.
• Creates a tight, leak-proof seal under pressure and temperature.

🔶 Real-Time Applications

• Flanged pipe connections in chemical plants and refineries
• Pressure vessels and heat exchangers
• Pumps, compressors, and engine components
• Any system where fluid or gas containment is crucial

⚠️ Critical Engineering Insight

Incorrect gasket selection or improper installation can lead to:

• Costly leaks and product loss
• Environmental contamination and safety hazards
• Equipment damage and operational downtime

Understanding gasket material compatibility (e.g., rubber, PTFE, metallic), temperature/pressure ratings, and correct bolt torque is essential for robust engineering design.

Follow for more insights into industrial components and plant operations.
