Citizen Science & AI: Empowering Indigenous Communities for Climate Resilience | Global Adaptation Insights,"Join us for a special 'Global Adaptation Insights' presentation, featuring Dr. Lena Khan, lead researcher at the Ethno-Environmental Data Collective. Dr. Khan discusses groundbreaking work in integrating traditional ecological knowledge (TEK) with modern citizen science and artificial intelligence platforms to build robust climate resilience strategies in indigenous communities worldwide.

Drawing on projects from the Amazon rainforest to the Arctic Circle, Dr. Khan's team demonstrates how community-led data collection, combined with advanced machine learning, can provide hyperlocal insights into environmental changes. This approach empowers communities not only to document impacts but also to co-design effective, culturally appropriate adaptation measures against compounding climate pressures.

Key discussion points include:
- Methodologies for ethically integrating traditional knowledge systems with digital data streams.
- The development of AI models for predictive analytics of biodiversity shifts, extreme weather events, and resource availability.
- Strategies for ensuring data sovereignty and equitable access to technological tools for indigenous groups.
- Case studies illustrating successful community-driven climate monitoring and adaptation initiatives.
- Navigating the challenges of technology transfer and sustaining digital infrastructure in remote areas.

This webinar is a part of the Global Climate Intelligence Network's 'Global Adaptation Insights' series, a free virtual event for environmental scientists, indigenous community leaders, data ethicists, policymakers, and NGOs exploring the frontiers of climate adaptation.",Global Climate Intelligence Network,95
