GATE Physics 2023 Solved Paper | Quantum Mechanics | COMPLETE Solution & Strategies,"If you are preparing for GATE Physics 2025, this video on Quantum Mechanics previous year questions (PYQs) will help you strengthen one of the most important sections for the exam.

Welcome to Part 7 of the GATE Quantum Mechanics Series, where we solve GATE Physics questions from 2010 to 2024 with detailed explanations and exam-oriented strategies.

⚛️ GATE Quantum Mechanics Syllabus
Wave-particle duality; Schrödinger equation (time-dependent and time-independent); Eigenvalue problems (particle in a box, harmonic oscillator, hydrogen atom); Tunneling through a barrier; Wave-function in coordinate and momentum space; Commutators and uncertainty principle; Dirac bra-ket notation; Pauli matrices; Spin angular momentum; Addition of angular momenta; Time-independent perturbation theory; Elementary scattering theory; Variational method.

📝 GATE 2025 Marking Scheme
GATE 2025 Physics is a 100-mark paper with 65 questions: 10 General Aptitude (15 marks) and 55 Subject Questions (85 marks). Subject questions include 1-mark and 2-mark MCQs (Multiple Choice Questions) and MSQs (Multiple Select Questions), and NATs (Numerical Answer Type Questions). Negative marking applies for MCQs (1/3 for 1-mark, 2/3 for 2-mark); no negative marking for MSQ and NAT questions.

