Spicy Crispy Chicken Spring Rolls with Creamy Avocado Dip Recipe | Party Appetizer!,"Spice up your party platter with these irresistible Spicy Crispy Chicken Spring Rolls! Paired with a cool, creamy avocado dip, they're sure to be a crowd-pleaser for any gathering – perfect for holidays, game nights, or just a fun family snack. #TheSavorySpot #PartyFood #CrispySpringRolls #ChickenRecipe #AvocadoDip #EasyAppetizer #FingerFood

Written recipe: (Link to blog post/website)

Ingredients for Spring Rolls:
- Chicken mince 300g
- Red onion, finely chopped 1/2 medium
- Green chilies, finely chopped 2-3 (adjust to taste)
- Ginger-garlic paste 1 tbsp
- Soy sauce 2 tbsp
- Sriracha or chili sauce 1 tbsp (adjust to taste)
- Cabbage, shredded 1 cup
- Carrot, shredded 1/2 cup
- Spring onion greens, chopped 1/4 cup
- Salt to taste
- Black pepper 1/2 tsp
- Spring roll wrappers 15-20 sheets
- Egg, whisked 1 (for sealing)
- Oil for deep frying

Ingredients for Creamy Avocado Dip:
- Ripe avocados 2 medium
- Greek yogurt or sour cream 1/4 cup
- Lime juice 1 tbsp
- Cilantro, fresh 2 tbsp, chopped
- Garlic clove, minced 1
- Salt to taste
- Black pepper to taste
- A pinch of cayenne pepper (optional)

Directions:
Prepare the Filling:
1. In a pan, heat a small amount of oil. Add finely chopped red onion and sauté until translucent.
2. Add ginger-garlic paste and green chilies, cook for 1 minute until fragrant.
3. Add chicken mince and cook until browned, breaking up any lumps.
4. Stir in soy sauce, sriracha, salt, and black pepper. Mix well.
5. Add shredded cabbage and carrot. Cook for 3-5 minutes until vegetables are slightly tender but still have a bite.
6. Stir in chopped spring onion greens. Remove from heat and let the filling cool completely.

Assemble the Spring Rolls:
1. Lay a spring roll wrapper on a clean surface with a corner pointing towards you.
2. Place a spoonful of cooled chicken filling near the bottom corner.
3. Fold the bottom corner over the filling.
4. Fold in the side corners towards the center.
5. Roll the wrapper tightly upwards towards the last corner.
6. Brush the last corner with whisked egg to seal the roll. Repeat with remaining filling and wrappers.

Fry the Spring Rolls:
1. Heat oil in a deep pan or wok to 170-175°C (340-350°F).
2. Carefully place spring rolls into the hot oil, frying in batches to avoid overcrowding.
3. Fry until golden brown and crispy on all sides, about 4-6 minutes per batch.
4. Remove with a slotted spoon and place on a wire rack lined with paper towels to drain excess oil.

Prepare the Creamy Avocado Dip:
1. In a food processor or blender, combine ripe avocados, Greek yogurt/sour cream, lime juice, fresh cilantro, minced garlic, salt, black pepper, and cayenne pepper (if using).
2. Blend until smooth and creamy. Taste and adjust seasonings as needed.

Serve:
- Serve the hot, crispy chicken spring rolls immediately with the cool, creamy avocado dip. Garnish with extra cilantro or a sprinkle of chili flakes if desired.",The Savory Spot,32500
