"GENERASI Z, BUZZER, DAN KECERDASAN DIGITAL: Menjaga Demokrasi di Era Algoritma","Di era digital yang serba cepat, Generasi Z menjadi garda terdepan dalam menghadapi arus informasi yang tak henti. Namun, bagaimana mereka menyaring informasi di tengah gempuran narasi buzzer dan algoritma yang dirancang untuk memecah belah? Apakah kecerdasan digital kita cukup untuk membentengi demokrasi? Diskusi mendalam ini mengungkap tantangan terbesar Gen Z dalam mengembangkan nalar kritis dan peran mereka dalam membentuk masa depan politik dan sosial Indonesia. Kita akan membahas mengapa kemampuan membedakan fakta dan fiksi bukan lagi pilihan, melainkan keharusan mutlak. Saksikan analisis tajam ini untuk memahami bagaimana kita bisa memberdayakan diri dan komunitas di tengah hiruk-pikuk dunia maya.",Nusantara Nalar,3500
ImmerseVest: Alpha | DIY Wireless Full-Body Haptic Suit for Gaming,"00:00 intro02:45 concept & ideation07:10 components & sourcing15:30 custom PCB design & assembly23:00 software & integration30:15 initial testing & calibration35:50 gameplay demo & feedback39:00 future plans & community callThis video sequentially walks through my ideation and build process for a DIY wireless full-body haptic feedback suit, totaling just $220. Notable features include 32 independently controllable haptic motors across the torso and limbs, low-latency wireless communication, and over four hours of battery life, all powered by a custom-designed PCB and open-source software. My focus with this Alpha phase was to prove the concept of a truly affordable and customizable haptic system, providing a robust, pre-optimized base for future iterations and more widespread adoption.The build turned out surprisingly well for a first prototype, exceeding my expectations for immersion and response time. This project was completed around January 2026 (video edited April 2026), and while sourcing individual components can be tricky, the core design aims for easily available and cost-effective parts. Bringing the total cost under $250 while delivering a compelling full-body experience is my highest priority.Since I'm now thrilled with the overall direction and the potential of the ImmerseVest, I will begin developing comprehensive written documentation and shareable design files in the next update. This will focus on a more modular and user-friendly design with improved ergonomics, advanced force feedback algorithms, and simplified assembly for other makers. The next iteration will also explore direct game integrations and perhaps even open API support. If there's anything specific you'd like to see included in the documentation or the next prototype, please mention it in the comments! Your feedback is invaluable as this is a community-driven project at heart.Video note: The audio recording was originally over 2.5 hours, but I've carefully edited out non-critical details and repetitive explanations (e.g., granular soldering techniques) to keep the video concise and focused on the core innovation.",ImmersionForge,18750
