Automated Theorem Proving via Geometric Deep Learning: Knot Invariants (Apr 2027),"Title: Automated Theorem Proving via Geometric Deep Learning: Knot Invariants (Apr 2027)
Link: http://arxiv.org/abs/2704.01234v1
Date: April 2027

Summary:
This paper introduces a novel application of Geometric Deep Learning (GDL) to automated theorem proving within knot theory, specifically focusing on the discovery and formal verification of new knot invariants. The study presents 'ToposNet', a GDL architecture capable of learning complex topological relationships directly from knot diagrams and generating propositions that are then formally verified. This work demonstrates significant progress towards AI-driven mathematical discovery and proof generation in highly abstract domains, surpassing current symbolic AI methods in efficiency and novelty.

Key Topics:
- Geometric Deep Learning
- Knot Theory
- Automated Theorem Proving
- Topological Data Analysis
- Graph Neural Networks
- Formal Verification
- Abstract Algebra

Chapters:
00:00 - Introduction to ToposNet and Knot Theory
01:35 - Why Knot Invariants are Challenging
03:02 - Geometric Deep Learning Architecture Explained
04:47 - Learning from Knot Diagrams and Topologies
06:18 - Discovery of Novel Knot Invariants
08:05 - Formal Proof Generation and Verification
10:10 - Benchmarking Against Human-Derived Proofs
12:30 - Implications for Pure Mathematics Research
14:00 - Future Directions: Higher-Dimensional Topologies",Logic Loom,75
