CyberPulse Update - 04/15/2026 - AI Deepfake Scam & Supply Chain Hack Shakes Tech,"In today's CyberPulse Update, we delve into two critical cybersecurity incidents making waves — a terrifying new AI-powered deepfake scam targeting corporate executives, and a widespread supply chain compromise impacting countless web applications.   STORY 1 — AI-POWERED VOICE DEEPFAKES EXTORTING CFOs (Project Echo) A sophisticated criminal syndicate, dubbed 'Project Echo,' is leveraging advanced AI voice synthesis to impersonate CEOs and high-ranking executives. Utilizing stolen corporate communications and publicly available audio, they create convincing deepfake voice calls to CFOs, urgently requesting fraudulent wire transfers or sensitive data. Initial reports indicate several successful incidents across financial and tech sectors, with one company losing $5 million. The attacks are highly targeted, often following extensive social engineering to gather intelligence on the executive's voice patterns and typical communication styles. Experts warn of a new era of 'auditory phishing' that bypasses traditional security checks.   STORY 2 — CRITICAL BACKDOOR FOUND IN WIDELY USED 'NETFLOW.JS' LIBRARY Security researchers have uncovered a state-sponsored backdoor embedded within 'NetFlow.js,' a popular open-source JavaScript library used for network traffic analysis in thousands of web applications and internal tools. The backdoor, active for over six months, allowed attackers to exfiltrate sensitive data, including API keys and user session tokens, from any application integrating the compromised version of the library. Organizations worldwide are scrambling to identify affected systems and patch immediately, fearing massive data breaches. This incident highlights the growing risks of supply chain attacks within the open-source ecosystem, even for seemingly innocuous utilities.   Sources: AI Deepfake Scam: https://www.cybertechdaily.com/aivoice-scam-alert/ NetFlow.js Backdoor: https://www.osssecurityinsights.org/netflowjs-compromise/   ByteBeat Daily provides cutting-edge cybersecurity news and analysis, keeping you ahead of the latest threats.  https://bytebeatdaily.com  #ByteBeatDaily #CyberPulse #CybersecurityNews #AIDeepfake #VoiceScam #ProjectEcho #SupplyChainAttack #NetFlowJS #OpenSourceSecurity #DataBreach #CyberCrime",ByteBeat Daily,35
