What Was The Luminiferous Aether? The Michelson-Morley Experiment Explained,"Before Einstein revolutionized our understanding of the universe, physicists believed in the 'luminiferous aether' – a mysterious medium thought to carry light waves through space. But in 1887, Albert Michelson and Edward Morley conducted a groundbreaking experiment that challenged this fundamental assumption. In this video, we dive into the history, setup, and shocking results of the Michelson-Morley experiment, a pivotal moment in physics that paved the way for Einstein's Special Relativity. Discover why their inability to detect the aether had profound implications for classical physics and forever changed our view of light and space. You will learn: • What the luminiferous aether was believed to be • The purpose and design of the Michelson-Morley interferometer • How the experiment was expected to detect Earth's motion through the aether • The unexpected 'null result' and its scientific impact • How this experiment provided crucial evidence for Special Relativity Understanding the Michelson-Morley experiment is essential for grasping the revolutionary leap from classical physics to modern concepts like the constancy of the speed of light. 📚 Perfect for: • Physics students and enthusiasts • High school & university learners studying relativity • Anyone interested in the history of science and groundbreaking experiments ✨ Keywords / Tags Michelson-Morley experiment, luminiferous aether, speed of light, special relativity, Einstein, classical physics, history of physics, interferometer, null result, physics education, relativity for beginners 🔔 If you enjoy explanations of fundamental physics concepts, like, subscribe, and turn on notifications for more videos on relativity, quantum mechanics, and cosmology.",PhysicsParadigm,85
