Algorithmic Bias Explained: Why Your AI Can Be Unfair & How to Fix It,"Algorithmic bias is one of the most critical and often overlooked challenges in Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning today. In this video, we break down what algorithmic bias is, how it silently creeps into AI systems, and why it's crucial for anyone working with or impacted by AI to understand it. You'll learn how machine learning models can perpetuate and even amplify existing societal biases through skewed training data, flawed algorithms, and human assumptions, leading to unfair or discriminatory outcomes in areas like hiring, lending, and criminal justice.

We'll explore practical strategies and ethical considerations to combat algorithmic bias, including data preprocessing techniques, fairness metrics, explainable AI (XAI) approaches, and the importance of diverse development teams. This beginner-friendly guide is essential for students, developers, data scientists, and anyone keen on building more responsible and equitable AI systems.

If you're interested in AI ethics, machine learning fairness, or responsible AI development, this video will provide foundational knowledge and actionable insights.

Topics Covered:
Algorithmic bias definition
AI ethics and fairness
Machine learning bias examples
Sources of bias in AI data
