18.2 NMR Spectroscopy: Proton NMR Explained (A-Level Chemistry),"In this A Level Chemistry lesson, experienced educator Professor Eleanor Vance demystifies one of the most powerful spectroscopic techniques for organic structure determination: Proton Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (¹H NMR) Spectroscopy.

¹H NMR spectroscopy provides invaluable information about the hydrogen atoms within a molecule, revealing details about their chemical environment and connectivity. It's an essential tool for organic chemists and a key topic for advanced chemistry students.

In this video you will learn:

⚛️ The fundamental principles of NMR – including nuclear spin, magnetic fields, and radio frequency absorption
 How chemical shift provides information about the electronic environment of protons
 Interpreting the number of proton environments from an NMR spectrum
 Understanding integration traces and what they reveal about the relative number of protons
 The 'n+1' rule for predicting splitting patterns (multiplicity) due to spin-spin coupling
 How to use the NMR data sheet and predict spectra for common organic compounds
 The significance of deuterium exchange in identifying acidic protons

Professor Vance works through several detailed examples of ¹H NMR spectra, demonstrating how to systematically deduce molecular structures from chemical shift, integration, and splitting data. This lesson is perfect for consolidating your understanding and mastering exam questions on spectroscopic analysis.

 Perfect for:
• AQA, OCR A, and Edexcel A Level Chemistry
• Revision of NMR spectroscopy and organic analysis
• Developing skills in spectral interpretation

Subscribe for more clear, concise, and exam-focused A Level Chemistry lessons from Prof. Chemistry Unlocked.

