Optimizing dbt Monorepos & Data Governance at Scale with Sarah Chen from DataForge Labs,"dbt isn't just about transformations. It's about building a reliable, governed data platform. In this episode, we dive deep into how effective data governance and performance optimization are crucial for large-scale dbt implementations. We’re joined by Sarah Chen, Principal Data Engineer at DataForge Labs, to discuss how her team manages sprawling dbt monorepos, implements robust data quality checks, and ensures consistent governance across hundreds of dbt models. From custom macro development for schema validation to CI/CD pipelines for model testing and strategies for optimizing dbt run times on massive datasets, this conversation covers practical engineering challenges and innovative solutions. Key Takeaways: 00:00 Introduction 01:15 How DataForge Labs leverages dbt for advanced analytics and machine learning features. 02:00 The complexities of managing a large dbt monorepo with multiple teams. 03:05 Designing a custom dbt package for automated data quality and validation checks. 04:20 Integrating dbt artifacts into a data catalog for automated lineage and metadata. 06:00 Strategies for optimizing dbt build and test performance on cloud data warehouses. 07:45 Enforcing data governance policies through dbt pre-commit hooks and CI pipelines. 09:10 The future of data observability and testing within the dbt ecosystem. Resources Mentioned: Sarah Chen https://www.linkedin.com/in/sarah-chen-dataeng/ DataForge Labs https://www.dataforgelabs.com/ dbt Labs https://www.getdbt.com/ Great Expectations https://greatexpectations.io/ Thanks for listening to “DataOps Deep Dive: Practical Strategies for Modern Data Platforms.” If you enjoyed this episode, please leave a 5-star review to help get the word out about the show. And be sure to subscribe so you never miss any of the insightful conversations. #dbt #DataEngineering #DataGovernance #AnalyticsEngineering #DataOps #SQL",DataOps Deep Dive,98
