The First Spacewalk: Voskhod 2 Mission Highlights (1965),"This documentary presents the key moments of the Voskhod 2 mission, a pivotal flight in the early Soviet space program. Launched on March 18, 1965, this mission made history when cosmonaut Alexei Leonov performed the first-ever spacewalk, venturing outside the spacecraft for 12 minutes.

The crew, comprised of Alexei Leonov (spacewalker) and Pavel Belyayev (commander), faced incredible challenges, most notably Leonov's space suit expanding in the vacuum of space, making his return to the capsule extremely difficult. Despite the dangers, this pioneering feat proved humanity's ability to operate in the harsh environment of open space, laying the groundwork for all future extravehicular activities.

This film compiles rare historical footage from Soviet archives, capturing the preparations, launch, the iconic spacewalk, and the triumphant, albeit challenging, return to Earth.

🚀 Historical Significance of the Voskhod 2 Mission:
*   First human spacewalk
*   Critical step in human space exploration
*   Demonstrated resilience and adaptability in extreme conditions

