Silencers in Movies: The Deafening Truth Hollywood Hides! #gunfacts #moviescience #mythbusting,"You've seen it countless times: a silent assassin dispatches targets with a whisper-quiet pistol, thanks to a sleek silencer. Hollywood loves this trope, but just like the Coriolis effect for snipers, it's a dramatic exaggeration! The truth about firearm suppressors is far from silent. They don't make guns whisper-quiet; they *reduce* the sound, often to the level of a jackhammer or a loud car backfiring. Why? Because the bullet still travels supersonically, creating a sonic boom, and gas still expands rapidly. Join us as we dismantle the silver screen fantasy and reveal the loud reality of gun suppressors. Your ears (and your understanding of physics) will thank you. #film #science #guns #suppressor #mythbusters #realsound",Reel Science,3875
