Why Does Ice Float on Water? 🧊 #sciencefacts #physics,"You've seen ice cubes bobbing in your drink, but have you ever wondered why they don't sink?
Most solids are denser than their liquid forms, causing them to sink. But water is an exception!
When water freezes, its molecules arrange themselves into a crystalline structure, which is more open and takes up more space than the liquid form. This means ice is less dense than liquid water.
This unique property is crucial for life on Earth, as it prevents entire bodies of water from freezing solid!
#ice #water #density #sciencefacts #howitworks #physics #chemistry #shorts #ytshorts #viralvideo",ScienceSimplified,215
