"Tinjau Ketersediaan & Harga Bahan Pokok Jelang Idul Adha, Walikota Bima Sidak Pasar Raya","Menjelang perayaan Idul Adha 1445 H, Walikota Bima, H. Muhammad Lutfi, S.E., didampingi Kepala Dinas Perdagangan dan Perindustrian, melakukan inspeksi mendadak (sidak) di Pasar Raya Bima. Sidak ini bertujuan untuk memantau ketersediaan pasokan bahan pokok serta stabilitas harga kebutuhan pangan seperti daging, telur, minyak goreng, dan beras, guna memastikan tidak ada kenaikan harga yang signifikan atau penimbunan. Walikota Lutfi berdialog langsung dengan para pedagang dan pembeli untuk mendengar masukan serta memastikan kelancaran distribusi. Hasil sidak menunjukkan pasokan masih aman dan harga cenderung stabil, namun tetap akan dipantau secara berkala hingga hari raya tiba. Langkah ini diambil untuk menjamin masyarakat dapat berbelanja dengan nyaman dan kebutuhan pangan terpenuhi selama periode hari raya.",Jelajah Kota Kita,850
Arduino Button Control: Your First Input! | Beginner Tutorial,"Ready to move beyond blinking lights? In this beginner-friendly tutorial, you'll learn how to connect a push-button to your Arduino and use it to control an LED. This project introduces you to reading digital input, a crucial skill for interactive Arduino projects.

What you'll learn:
• How to wire a push-button with a pull-down resistor
• Reading digital input from an Arduino pin
• Controlling an LED based on button presses
• Basic digital input Arduino code
• Uploading your code and seeing it in action

This tutorial is perfect for anyone who has completed the 'LED Blink' project and is looking to add interactivity to their electronics.

Components used:
• Arduino Uno
• Push Button
• LED
• 220Ω Resistor
• 10kΩ Resistor (for pull-down)
• Jumper wires
• Breadboard

Arduino Button Control Code:

```cpp
const int buttonPin = 2;   // the number of the pushbutton pin
const int ledPin = 13;     // the number of the LED pin

void setup() {
  pinMode(buttonPin, INPUT);
  pinMode(ledPin, OUTPUT);
}

void loop() {
  int buttonState = digitalRead(buttonPin); // read the state of the pushbutton value

  if (buttonState == HIGH) { // check if the pushbutton is pressed.
    digitalWrite(ledPin, HIGH); // turn LED on
  } else {
    digitalWrite(ledPin, LOW);  // turn LED off
  }
}
```

If you found this video helpful, please like, share, and subscribe to our channel for more exciting Arduino projects and tutorials!

