The Secret Continent You've Never Seen #Shorts,"Meet Zealandia: Earth's almost entirely submerged eighth continent #Shorts
The Massive Landmass Hiding Under The Pacific #Shorts

Around 85 million years ago, a colossal landmass the size of India began to separate from the supercontinent Gondwana. This isn't merely a large island; it possesses all the definitive geological characteristics of a true continent, including a diverse geology, a well-defined area distinctly separate from oceanic crust, and a crustal thickness greater than oceanic crust. Today, over 94% of this continent, officially dubbed Zealandia, lies profoundly beneath the waves of the Pacific Ocean, with New Zealand and New Caledonia being its most prominent above-water parts. Geologists officially recognized Zealandia as Earth's eighth continent in 2017, profoundly challenging our conventional understanding of global geography. Its recognition highlights the dynamic nature of our planet's crust and the ongoing processes of plate tectonics and continental drift, revealing a hidden chapter in Earth's deep history right beneath our oceans. It's a profound reminder that much of our world remains undiscovered, even on a continental scale.",Deep Earth Chronicles,16500
